[{"sha":"515f7054265806325ff9f3d6c938770daacd1678","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUxNWY3MDU0MjY1ODA2MzI1ZmY5ZjNkNmM5Mzg3NzBkYWFjZDE2Nzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alex Daley","email":"adaley@openai.com","date":"2026-06-16T00:08:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T00:08:39Z"},"message":"[codex] Fix missing response item metadata in tests (#28415)\n\nSummary\n- Add the two missing `metadata: None` initializers after #28355 made\nresponse-item metadata required.\n- Restore test compilation for `codex-core` and `codex-api` on main.\n\nValidation\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just fmt` (Rust formatting passed; unrelated Python formatter steps\ncould not use the sandboxed shared `uv` cache)\n- Focused crate tests are running after PR creation.","tree":{"sha":"c3751983590daf7719ecf174805b4978183c087c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c3751983590daf7719ecf174805b4978183c087c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/515f7054265806325ff9f3d6c938770daacd1678","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMJQHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOeMQAIgP8YOOfTfkzB4etmvkyz5L\nLk47ZOPT27F/sgdtW8vnkqXGLiOaGeAfh0OW9xFdWUszDIE779BRFHxRax9xLZGV\nTh1F5vLVad/SkHIyISUW2FrtcZ5tzIAR4DYBrMy45+mOp9/eHKCdSaolaPOj9pF3\n/Pm84svyJ95VG3uFPvF8LiILygnXqb4KBly52mTZE+VbjbBfWqUHYUupEBvfzt9i\nxYglfxd4AYhoQ26M+GA4gv5fv7w0oF1FIW0ZwGgO6bsgSWr2tA/qXuFjJDe1FpgH\nd3wVyiwfGYApxclnR+TuIzrI+GThtT1yBiLS4arTWOzbc5Vizldfljs67vUoVOeh\ndmK2T9kIBqda3YKo6kbbZEFiUjsSLxkzYKfCeaWYqdSq3ON9h+BsFTmjGGJENZb3\nv5dLMjSCysYZIHpccUEdbrdrNbB6KvhT/gNlWkV/gCpBQzGY1q0fZtjxcvV6lL2f\nHQnH2K7xsGIGOikIoI+FM5gA52PsHH9ZDV1UHjO/kHSd3WcpI0Ne+R7bfIQx9ehQ\ne1rOcqgUtve9HcpyRUVwPdnPLMkeG1JrwfoxdxTzV5b0fnh41KuWbkmAUGfUD3fE\nkkh3BVJ6ZxuFRdXpUYcDXPgKTXZqS7sbZzPftLZ0hcGf+U5A6LHmSaII+j5EjREo\nPdC3CdhUb7VaPc+3ge1L\n=7vaX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c3751983590daf7719ecf174805b4978183c087c\nparent 46f17930b64b3f237a6d87207b5b2138881d5a74\nauthor Alex Daley <adaley@openai.com> 1781568519 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781568519 +0000\n\n[codex] Fix missing response item metadata in tests (#28415)\n\nSummary\n- Add the two missing `metadata: None` initializers after #28355 made\nresponse-item metadata required.\n- Restore test compilation for `codex-core` and `codex-api` on main.\n\nValidation\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just fmt` (Rust formatting passed; unrelated Python formatter steps\ncould not use the sandboxed shared `uv` cache)\n- Focused crate tests are running after PR creation.","verified_at":"2026-06-16T00:08:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/515f7054265806325ff9f3d6c938770daacd1678","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/515f7054265806325ff9f3d6c938770daacd1678","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/515f7054265806325ff9f3d6c938770daacd1678/comments","author":{"login":"adaley-openai","id":192042180,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3JUxA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192042180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/adaley-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"46f17930b64b3f237a6d87207b5b2138881d5a74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/46f17930b64b3f237a6d87207b5b2138881d5a74","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/46f17930b64b3f237a6d87207b5b2138881d5a74"}]},{"sha":"46f17930b64b3f237a6d87207b5b2138881d5a74","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ2ZjE3OTMwYjY0YjNmMjM3YTZkODcyMDdiNWIyMTM4ODgxZDVhNzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:55:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:55:23Z"},"message":"Use PathUri in filesystem permission paths for exec-server (#28165)\n\n## Why\n\nProgress towards letting app-server and exec-server run on different\nplatforms, specifically for sandbox configuration.\n\n## What\n\n- Make the filesystem path containment hierarchy generic, defaulting to\n`AbsolutePathBuf` for now.\n- Have clients specify `AbsolutePathBuf` or `PathUri` directly where\nneeded.\n- Use `PathUri` throughout exec-server filesystem protocol and trait\nboundaries.\n- Implement `From` for conversion to path URIs and `TryFrom` for\nfallible conversion to absolute paths through the generic type\nhierarchy.","tree":{"sha":"3e3680bfe0247aca8e6ad21eae3a4dff0a72633b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3e3680bfe0247aca8e6ad21eae3a4dff0a72633b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/46f17930b64b3f237a6d87207b5b2138881d5a74","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMJDrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHNUQAHbyiNei9Z650228Vdp8uWtl\nVJfdgE4EIYU0c3StAqlHw+UI4pUUTrH/r95igy/GiUz+M1zR2kAZQ/VvJwPh3F0m\n90hJfnw6og5Qy6KZ1nOW1A5ujBAEi5KqfSlSWuirbFt49wHSNJFSvBNyV9/g+DyQ\nnA67wSpF3/2CsrwVoalnskr3xKFDVxQYxytiuHA9Ktur9mCMY0SlzfwQNKqHmZzU\n+WPl1VW7ZFXAgonhaT8ox1h/GgC/N54ZMO9B9GBarxY0WtSPwd07oRSKJcFvhNha\ng3vCThmviuTvjksYXpmEvkTkMRZPCdP7ZsTQrPg81RemNeoAT1j+0ZhaOEyHfanC\nr7gPWayJcfWCu72eRvxdZ8fZaQApOQk8kkenp0zlVl7jJ4fN+69XO0EjkjJNA3rO\ntSTB8AxnHkf/w4bd+umQseFQJxLdkh7w7kCoCTeSYSmleJw8O+2hteRmAWmfbRqz\n8grdoDGRDfcSiFSsC/JLevTO3cRSZrLZWxzB/XnFMYkO7ckTjXn8uVecADmWPJbW\ncwI8yUKRiWYr7x8xbmZpLIr9pR9TUJ5+Tgwx3Jh4AswaOQsygjwKrFwkNeoRJdW+\n1Mu0/vPpuyBDdqMHCfL+LmC1Bgsr5IlFUhi1VYA7nGHIcbfo3Xjl+wQtxsmbNIzD\nij7ApW+OL2BPWlSsZtV5\n=sZdy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3e3680bfe0247aca8e6ad21eae3a4dff0a72633b\nparent 428cd44154b5a5b3f1edb4f6c7603648777faffa\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781567723 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781567723 +0000\n\nUse PathUri in filesystem permission paths for exec-server (#28165)\n\n## Why\n\nProgress towards letting app-server and exec-server run on different\nplatforms, specifically for sandbox configuration.\n\n## What\n\n- Make the filesystem path containment hierarchy generic, defaulting to\n`AbsolutePathBuf` for now.\n- Have clients specify `AbsolutePathBuf` or `PathUri` directly where\nneeded.\n- Use `PathUri` throughout exec-server filesystem protocol and trait\nboundaries.\n- Implement `From` for conversion to path URIs and `TryFrom` for\nfallible conversion to absolute paths through the generic type\nhierarchy.","verified_at":"2026-06-15T23:55:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/46f17930b64b3f237a6d87207b5b2138881d5a74","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/46f17930b64b3f237a6d87207b5b2138881d5a74","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/46f17930b64b3f237a6d87207b5b2138881d5a74/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"428cd44154b5a5b3f1edb4f6c7603648777faffa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/428cd44154b5a5b3f1edb4f6c7603648777faffa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/428cd44154b5a5b3f1edb4f6c7603648777faffa"}]},{"sha":"428cd44154b5a5b3f1edb4f6c7603648777faffa","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQyOGNkNDQxNTRiNWE1YjNmMWVkYjRmNmM3NjAzNjQ4Nzc3ZmFmZmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:39:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:39:41Z"},"message":"exec-server: add Noise relay transport (#26242)\n\n## Why\n\nRendezvous forwards traffic between the orchestrator and exec-server.\nThe endpoints need to authenticate each other and encrypt that traffic\nwithout trusting Rendezvous with plaintext or endpoint keys.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Adds a hybrid Noise IK channel through Clatter using X25519,\nML-KEM-768, AES-256-GCM, and SHA-256.\n- Binds each handshake to `environment_id`, `executor_registration_id`,\nand `stream_id`.\n- Pins the registry-provided executor key and carries the harness\nauthorization inside the encrypted handshake.\n- Orders relay frames before consuming Noise nonces and fragments large\nJSON-RPC messages into bounded records.\n- Bounds handshake payloads, frames, streams, and message reassembly.\n\nRuntime activation is in\n[openai/codex#26245](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26245).\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **[openai/codex#26242](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26242)**:\nNoise channel and relay transport\n2. [openai/codex#26245](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26245):\nremote registration and runtime activation\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server`\n- Oversized initiator payload regression coverage\n- `just fix -p codex-exec-server`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `cargo shear`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"146746d25607048e77a61dc14ec4932a28a4601f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/146746d25607048e77a61dc14ec4932a28a4601f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/428cd44154b5a5b3f1edb4f6c7603648777faffa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMI09CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGv4QAGM56fRw8fQU9vRqL6EcSCZj\nJAv8x3etxtWTPaoUA0CwsrdndAU6SGSKC2OCB/1npng4CvAotc6IGAYH9smydHwV\nPdavoLobwsdJrD3V/u56rw7R7Lfuzgfjv8UqTh1qhOw3ZvXZwPlyHBGrMedM38mP\nlaaRkLe9HNJh/sf7HBDGLHS5m+o9R8JgXgo6uR3/8wOUL/nIbTp3mhCrklAKErrL\n28Rat/13ueR64BI7Of+t80K8zC6Ufg11X1/9NBwULc13qQESoSmuI6u9nxSG90WQ\nQ7H0FhzOtddtdyYshP+B5p2BuuY973d9d6jRb7v4dETcGL7wwHiiU01/Bu5D5NHn\nUZe3r283p/kC3TE8EEyDuR+zsI12GSjo6q55x+wFlVeYlUj8h/XVU2yEdcavyayt\nEnIrjTPS19NkaB/k+P0NjYe8xvcyalhIVs5B6HJyJXglphVfDxQCgj24Vlp1x3MF\ncT05viq9LdKpcv9XjY0ZpE1eQx0WaQywju/Kj3XlF0M2OIK2WSRwShuQ+o0++GVa\nHTKrDLYvc14tyPHzvl3ZPi4SvlaQ/v6utlf4DVmCoVdUOxDZD6f/sV0eFnBAOBCc\nlAh3Y123tTcoLPZ9pPiOnrQMgBp/mFCi0oq2AtuNQuLYMS1DkxrZg5X/mRt95851\n7npKvzoyNRFkvpXicRCQ\n=WkO0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 146746d25607048e77a61dc14ec4932a28a4601f\nparent e512e884ed7f4cab9a36ed158013a273b990f078\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1781566781 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781566781 -0700\n\nexec-server: add Noise relay transport (#26242)\n\n## Why\n\nRendezvous forwards traffic between the orchestrator and exec-server.\nThe endpoints need to authenticate each other and encrypt that traffic\nwithout trusting Rendezvous with plaintext or endpoint keys.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Adds a hybrid Noise IK channel through Clatter using X25519,\nML-KEM-768, AES-256-GCM, and SHA-256.\n- Binds each handshake to `environment_id`, `executor_registration_id`,\nand `stream_id`.\n- Pins the registry-provided executor key and carries the harness\nauthorization inside the encrypted handshake.\n- Orders relay frames before consuming Noise nonces and fragments large\nJSON-RPC messages into bounded records.\n- Bounds handshake payloads, frames, streams, and message reassembly.\n\nRuntime activation is in\n[openai/codex#26245](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26245).\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **[openai/codex#26242](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26242)**:\nNoise channel and relay transport\n2. [openai/codex#26245](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26245):\nremote registration and runtime activation\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server`\n- Oversized initiator payload regression coverage\n- `just fix -p codex-exec-server`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `cargo shear`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T23:39:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/428cd44154b5a5b3f1edb4f6c7603648777faffa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/428cd44154b5a5b3f1edb4f6c7603648777faffa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/428cd44154b5a5b3f1edb4f6c7603648777faffa/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e512e884ed7f4cab9a36ed158013a273b990f078","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e512e884ed7f4cab9a36ed158013a273b990f078","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e512e884ed7f4cab9a36ed158013a273b990f078"}]},{"sha":"e512e884ed7f4cab9a36ed158013a273b990f078","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU1MTJlODg0ZWQ3ZjRjYWI5YTM2ZWQxNTgwMTNhMjczYjk5MGYwNzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jameswt-oai","email":"jameswt@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:32:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:32:38Z"},"message":"[codex-analytics] Analytics Capture to File in Debug Builds (#27093)\n\n## This PR\n\nThe original [combined remote plugin analytics PR\n#26281](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26281) mixed reusable\nanalytics test infrastructure, two manual smoke workflows, a metadata\nrefactor, and the final identity behavior. This PR isolates the generic\ncapture mechanism so it can be reviewed and landed before any\nplugin-specific behavior.\n\n- Add a debug-only analytics destination that writes final request\npayloads as JSONL.\n- Suppress HTTP delivery whenever capture mode is selected, including\nafter capture write failures.\n- Keep release behavior unchanged even when the capture environment\nvariable is present.\n- Keep the mechanism generic; this PR contains no plugin-specific\nbehavior.\n\nSet `CODEX_ANALYTICS_EVENTS_CAPTURE_FILE=/path/events.jsonl` when\nrunning a debug Codex binary to inspect the exact batched payload that\nwould otherwise be sent to the analytics endpoint.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-analytics` (76 passed)\n- `just test --release -p codex-analytics` (73 passed)\n- CI is green across the required platform matrix.\n\n## Split Overview\n\n```text\nmain\n├── #27093  Debug analytics capture                 ← you are here\n│   └── #27099  Non-mutating plugin smoke\n│       └── #27100  Remote install/uninstall smoke\n└── #27102  Plugin telemetry metadata refactor\n\nAfter #27093, #27099, #27100, and #27102 merge:\n└── Final PR: add remote_plugin_id to plugin analytics\n```\n\nReview order and dependencies:\n\n1. [#27093 Add debug-only analytics event\ncapture](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27093) **(this PR, based\non `main`)**\n2. [#27099 Add a plugin analytics smoke\nworkflow](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27099) (stacked on\n#27093)\n3. [#27100 Add a remote plugin analytics mutation smoke\nworkflow](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27100) (stacked on\n#27099)\n4. [#27102 Centralize plugin telemetry metadata\nconstruction](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27102) (independent,\nbased on `main`)\n5. Final remote-ID behavior PR (created after PRs 1-4 merge)\n\nThe original [#26281](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26281)\nremains open as the green aggregate reference until the final PR is\npublished.","tree":{"sha":"dcc341ef23215856749d3794b7a78f270c2d6dee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/dcc341ef23215856749d3794b7a78f270c2d6dee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e512e884ed7f4cab9a36ed158013a273b990f078","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMIuWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARFAQAG7Q934r12I/s/77AvB9oYJX\n8tgOvHkwK31DZezJEsvqIW63MGCSBpN7tjEze2CIEFzVeXKFBRapMHFx0hhAjjnr\nDMid77pBat26KrA6D16FnjuNHLt9Boau0iecuArLJkvaTKmDIrRNtk9rA1oDlPXt\nFr4/FtWu5L/guarbUAKmRnHVLTxw/B2/oVYGoc9apbo6tFRR5Hh16MtN+bVMGv5V\nG3pRKmVPUhxUR6DBU4hU8pdLa2I8g5AXa+PiLpXYofLMMVdQDf2DrK6yc3MvouOa\nHQxSurMS6/NNehu8ekdlCIezGgGBtaGMpepmNSMaRh3DpM9qtV5FXGmApCW2bNvK\nWi5yFVx3NAz3qRXlSYwztDtZHLHH24xJNzb8y6CqVk6PT1w8/D4MpkrMpi2gq16z\nsAwkcyFfzzZ7wWGpQSkarJwAzEOG+/NaLig58hQbQZbxhTDDuyQOjYcr+4HmTtbg\nJlfkdLcMTd5dl6inbaC0aTy6DNRVWeg+KC5qNHxJo5M+2yuQLIUjibQkkxCIPe55\nmxx2CUj03RQuPipF+A8Fx6FRwA3uVOpQg0qSIFIWwjje8scUM2vWUXaTPNJH25Fu\nMBIv6w/wLpHJAQ60RVHKGSPXiKkUU5EKJIwSpMr3/K6b171mcgTjYGRZ4M9ZDkOF\nATtp+ZBPv9yDejkuUabj\n=XWe4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dcc341ef23215856749d3794b7a78f270c2d6dee\nparent 1d8ff89aa3808e364918bdec56d3cdfd74bf4d7b\nauthor jameswt-oai <jameswt@openai.com> 1781566358 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781566358 -0700\n\n[codex-analytics] Analytics Capture to File in Debug Builds (#27093)\n\n## This PR\n\nThe original [combined remote plugin analytics PR\n#26281](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26281) mixed reusable\nanalytics test infrastructure, two manual smoke workflows, a metadata\nrefactor, and the final identity behavior. This PR isolates the generic\ncapture mechanism so it can be reviewed and landed before any\nplugin-specific behavior.\n\n- Add a debug-only analytics destination that writes final request\npayloads as JSONL.\n- Suppress HTTP delivery whenever capture mode is selected, including\nafter capture write failures.\n- Keep release behavior unchanged even when the capture environment\nvariable is present.\n- Keep the mechanism generic; this PR contains no plugin-specific\nbehavior.\n\nSet `CODEX_ANALYTICS_EVENTS_CAPTURE_FILE=/path/events.jsonl` when\nrunning a debug Codex binary to inspect the exact batched payload that\nwould otherwise be sent to the analytics endpoint.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-analytics` (76 passed)\n- `just test --release -p codex-analytics` (73 passed)\n- CI is green across the required platform matrix.\n\n## Split Overview\n\n```text\nmain\n├── #27093  Debug analytics capture                 ← you are here\n│   └── #27099  Non-mutating plugin smoke\n│       └── #27100  Remote install/uninstall smoke\n└── #27102  Plugin telemetry metadata refactor\n\nAfter #27093, #27099, #27100, and #27102 merge:\n└── Final PR: add remote_plugin_id to plugin analytics\n```\n\nReview order and dependencies:\n\n1. [#27093 Add debug-only analytics event\ncapture](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27093) **(this PR, based\non `main`)**\n2. [#27099 Add a plugin analytics smoke\nworkflow](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27099) (stacked on\n#27093)\n3. [#27100 Add a remote plugin analytics mutation smoke\nworkflow](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27100) (stacked on\n#27099)\n4. [#27102 Centralize plugin telemetry metadata\nconstruction](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27102) (independent,\nbased on `main`)\n5. Final remote-ID behavior PR (created after PRs 1-4 merge)\n\nThe original [#26281](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26281)\nremains open as the green aggregate reference until the final PR is\npublished.","verified_at":"2026-06-15T23:32:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e512e884ed7f4cab9a36ed158013a273b990f078","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e512e884ed7f4cab9a36ed158013a273b990f078","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e512e884ed7f4cab9a36ed158013a273b990f078/comments","author":{"login":"jameswt-oai","id":247462917,"node_id":"U_kgDODr_8BQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247462917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jameswt-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1d8ff89aa3808e364918bdec56d3cdfd74bf4d7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1d8ff89aa3808e364918bdec56d3cdfd74bf4d7b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1d8ff89aa3808e364918bdec56d3cdfd74bf4d7b"}]},{"sha":"1d8ff89aa3808e364918bdec56d3cdfd74bf4d7b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFkOGZmODlhYTM4MDhlMzY0OTE4YmRlYzU2ZDNjZGZkNzRiZjRkN2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"guinness-oai","email":"guinness@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:15:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:15:58Z"},"message":"Add realtime speech append control (#27917)\n\n## Why\n\nRealtime voice harness tuning needs app-side control over what backend\nCodex text is spoken. Backend orchestrator text is written for a reading\nUI, so automatically speaking every preamble, progress update, or final\nassistant message can make the realtime voice model too chatty.\n\nFor experimentation, clients need two simple controls: keep app/client\ntext-item injection on the existing item-create path, and add an\nexplicit speakable path that app code can call only when it wants\nrealtime to speak. Automatic Codex output also needs an opt-in way to\nswitch from the protocol's default speakable path to regular realtime\nitems, with a caller-provided prefix so prompt wording can be tuned\noutside core.\n\nThe default remains unchanged: if a client omits the new start fields\nand never calls `appendSpeech`, automatic backend output continues down\nthe existing speakable path for the selected realtime protocol.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds experimental `thread/realtime/appendSpeech` for app-provided\nspeakable text.\n- Keeps existing `thread/realtime/appendText` as the item-create API for\napp-provided realtime text items.\n- Adds `codexResponsesAsItems` / `codex_responses_as_items` on\n`thread/realtime/start` to send automatic Codex responses with\n`conversation.item.create` instead of the protocol's default speakable\noutput path.\n- Adds `codexResponseItemPrefix` / `codex_response_item_prefix` so\nclients can prepend experiment instructions to those automatic Codex\nresponse items.\n- Keeps literal `conversation.handoff.append` routing scoped to the v1\nspeakable path; v2 default speech uses its item/function-output plus\n`response.create` behavior.\n- Removes the earlier public silent-context API and hardcoded\nsilent-context prefix.\n- Updates realtime tests to cover default automatic speakable behavior,\nopt-in automatic item-create behavior, and explicit `appendSpeech`\nbehavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-core -p codex-app-server -p codex-api`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server realtime_conversation`\n- `just test -p codex-core realtime_conversation` (50/51 passed in the\nfiltered parallel run; the lone failure passed when rerun in isolation)\n- `just test -p codex-core\nconversation_mirrors_assistant_message_text_to_realtime_handoff`\n- `just test -p codex-api\ne2e_connect_and_exchange_events_against_mock_ws_server`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`\n- `cargo build -p codex-cli`","tree":{"sha":"a16c78be66e1e91e8c5a3226665201a66c1e43d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a16c78be66e1e91e8c5a3226665201a66c1e43d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1d8ff89aa3808e364918bdec56d3cdfd74bf4d7b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMIeuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYY0QAF5oJyPzrRF+czfnybbwBvMU\nKuerYpFua5jI3c8QxvJghos/8hCRQzaqDLLuVw+DszLyaOoGgVUslCfM3BwZJcFz\ndyEOtbtY/9uedbK7BQsUefOZM/r4MWq/wBgQTEe3GjAIGp5QEKHa0VO9k7H06VWD\nvNtT7yWAY3E5ftATYItCk/MyU8sBkC3OKiODaFjlFH0nZUCTJHNxcYeKrAbKY9Dc\nFp5COfo1WM7qrn6Ycugfp1CAHQvYwnKGc2aAT91RQwwykm9/xuUPb+U1ScJjfErD\nctRXpKVrnaXrqx0G/vZuY3U5iZfYW4oqO6lYw8n9pATXKvrfybpsq0Y4Uc3KkKt/\nXN4yoGvy0b4P+R0G1C9wTLHVdv5sfRc5mnJ/IyevTCFR3nPwwzKaRbxdHDpp43kY\nfPSvw4ABNQX1i/eC/aeGXFbgNWUke1IU8xfI9JQ7l9TkVwWWvgqwOQZYLIAgCcg6\nadWZ3Ps6Z+zdlq8kzeRiNbMRcF2N9I6miW9r8Z4kr/FZyifHrobnBuaGPDyvKGVv\njd/nlBRu2Zt4AUENL54RYOg7LK39UGGi2KSMTD9LGPUa6+Mg5yMCBz54IHATkH27\nCTDhJZWFHeqacm2uFaC3wDo5BBCydR+aGFzNCfe47Q49iqqAPEZcU7CGT5UxULvt\n/BjJ+3c2MrdkGAwjyweb\n=HT9d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a16c78be66e1e91e8c5a3226665201a66c1e43d4\nparent 9728992fab1aaba5d1ca801f22402b7c8c3e5760\nauthor guinness-oai <guinness@openai.com> 1781565358 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781565358 -0700\n\nAdd realtime speech append control (#27917)\n\n## Why\n\nRealtime voice harness tuning needs app-side control over what backend\nCodex text is spoken. Backend orchestrator text is written for a reading\nUI, so automatically speaking every preamble, progress update, or final\nassistant message can make the realtime voice model too chatty.\n\nFor experimentation, clients need two simple controls: keep app/client\ntext-item injection on the existing item-create path, and add an\nexplicit speakable path that app code can call only when it wants\nrealtime to speak. Automatic Codex output also needs an opt-in way to\nswitch from the protocol's default speakable path to regular realtime\nitems, with a caller-provided prefix so prompt wording can be tuned\noutside core.\n\nThe default remains unchanged: if a client omits the new start fields\nand never calls `appendSpeech`, automatic backend output continues down\nthe existing speakable path for the selected realtime protocol.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds experimental `thread/realtime/appendSpeech` for app-provided\nspeakable text.\n- Keeps existing `thread/realtime/appendText` as the item-create API for\napp-provided realtime text items.\n- Adds `codexResponsesAsItems` / `codex_responses_as_items` on\n`thread/realtime/start` to send automatic Codex responses with\n`conversation.item.create` instead of the protocol's default speakable\noutput path.\n- Adds `codexResponseItemPrefix` / `codex_response_item_prefix` so\nclients can prepend experiment instructions to those automatic Codex\nresponse items.\n- Keeps literal `conversation.handoff.append` routing scoped to the v1\nspeakable path; v2 default speech uses its item/function-output plus\n`response.create` behavior.\n- Removes the earlier public silent-context API and hardcoded\nsilent-context prefix.\n- Updates realtime tests to cover default automatic speakable behavior,\nopt-in automatic item-create behavior, and explicit `appendSpeech`\nbehavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-core -p codex-app-server -p codex-api`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server realtime_conversation`\n- `just test -p codex-core realtime_conversation` (50/51 passed in the\nfiltered parallel run; the lone failure passed when rerun in isolation)\n- `just test -p codex-core\nconversation_mirrors_assistant_message_text_to_realtime_handoff`\n- `just test -p codex-api\ne2e_connect_and_exchange_events_against_mock_ws_server`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`\n- `cargo build -p codex-cli`","verified_at":"2026-06-15T23:15:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1d8ff89aa3808e364918bdec56d3cdfd74bf4d7b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1d8ff89aa3808e364918bdec56d3cdfd74bf4d7b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1d8ff89aa3808e364918bdec56d3cdfd74bf4d7b/comments","author":{"login":"guinness-oai","id":254771997,"node_id":"U_kgDODy-DHQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254771997?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/guinness-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9728992fab1aaba5d1ca801f22402b7c8c3e5760","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9728992fab1aaba5d1ca801f22402b7c8c3e5760","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9728992fab1aaba5d1ca801f22402b7c8c3e5760"}]},{"sha":"9728992fab1aaba5d1ca801f22402b7c8c3e5760","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk3Mjg5OTJmYWIxYWFiYTVkMWNhODAxZjIyNDAyYjdjOGMzZTU3NjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:15:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:15:07Z"},"message":"[codex] retain resolved environments across turns (#27955)\n\n## Why\n\nSelected execution environments are thread-scoped resources, but startup\nand turn construction repeatedly resolved their IDs and working\ndirectories. That discarded existing environment handles and shell\nmetadata even when a selection had not changed.\n\nSession configuration updates also need to affect future turns without\nchanging the resolved environment set already captured by a running\nturn.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Create a `ThreadEnvironments` service inside `Codex` from the spawned\n`EnvironmentManager` and raw environment selections, then store it on\n`SessionServices`.\n- Split service construction from `update_selections`, allowing session\nconfiguration updates to mutate the resolved set in place.\n- Retain an existing `TurnEnvironment` when its environment ID and\nworking directory match; resolve only added or changed selections and\nremove selections that are no longer present.\n- Normalize duplicate IDs by keeping the first selection and skip\nindividual selections that fail to resolve instead of rejecting the\nentire update.\n- Give each `TurnContext` a cloned `TurnEnvironmentSnapshot`, so later\nsession configuration updates affect future turns without rewriting an\nactive turn.\n- Reuse the service-owned environment manager and resolved snapshot for\nstartup work, MCP initialization, and child-thread spawning instead of\nflowing resolved environments through spawn arguments.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-core --tests`\n- `just test -p codex-core environment_selection`\n- `just test -p codex-core turn_environments`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsession_update_settings_does_not_rewrite_sticky_environment_cwds`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndefault_turn_does_not_overlay_legacy_fallback_cwd_onto_stored_thread_environments`","tree":{"sha":"d8871b63b9ea85d61b7be5cf846fd28f4897a0be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d8871b63b9ea85d61b7be5cf846fd28f4897a0be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9728992fab1aaba5d1ca801f22402b7c8c3e5760","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMId7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArcQQABRlZr/ylRLRjwJE1CHsy+x0\n2LYd+rvlkOJZbueH5Liw5MVbeQqlgxr6IKEpqE4CBFIbfZvzhDsw9mD8LOgMNef6\nH9jvLjJjB09QrdMyefwC0O+M54p0YqQ+M7DnMm38wizGE/tEThhEGzXDjopksTyp\nKAlj/vcHNiW+902sI3DyGqbdfWY2HHr3mfs3y/VS1YLaaQCX2lTBGw/RUET9t6DE\nibB+sKU1FO+6sArRtE84ikwKVoO90tYIUi69c9Yu0zHc4BQ24fJaHCdNG/T8EdrN\niGCD6PpB2UnkBDf+QEoS9ZTRP1onI3P7bP1NP0eAfoNq+pyUsvGB80zZlXhXBHG4\nJqmVrDT56iC6YMKmLL1gfpNbad6sYwS8NRSUNDKQQQ7QRr47ww453ycfQPsO9hHC\nu8VCN9OD5V6MjK0miGRLaNrVGxNqOn5RjnLMENSmV/AeS73AAjghTB7ZoDRAm4zq\nMB8+wSNkHieRfoGTov1yMpe2PIXJiQW9jMFWp8shXO9YFRn2CDTNGd0YvB+LiP/v\n2RJbLkb6MeS+TyUzf2PkdwMTac9TAw4r5uax8sRHum2E0tVnsqEKkf22BZ1+S9ZU\nV5Dz/lyRCe+Tmiuy7+NHsvmy25A06VVOYlP8C7xwddU+Y+NunzjhPBZ5YVkH3W39\nieW/n3UtuSq4BG/DrS6j\n=2WFK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d8871b63b9ea85d61b7be5cf846fd28f4897a0be\nparent 4c1c9bf327e33fc18cf64af54bf706101659511d\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781565307 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781565307 -0700\n\n[codex] retain resolved environments across turns (#27955)\n\n## Why\n\nSelected execution environments are thread-scoped resources, but startup\nand turn construction repeatedly resolved their IDs and working\ndirectories. That discarded existing environment handles and shell\nmetadata even when a selection had not changed.\n\nSession configuration updates also need to affect future turns without\nchanging the resolved environment set already captured by a running\nturn.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Create a `ThreadEnvironments` service inside `Codex` from the spawned\n`EnvironmentManager` and raw environment selections, then store it on\n`SessionServices`.\n- Split service construction from `update_selections`, allowing session\nconfiguration updates to mutate the resolved set in place.\n- Retain an existing `TurnEnvironment` when its environment ID and\nworking directory match; resolve only added or changed selections and\nremove selections that are no longer present.\n- Normalize duplicate IDs by keeping the first selection and skip\nindividual selections that fail to resolve instead of rejecting the\nentire update.\n- Give each `TurnContext` a cloned `TurnEnvironmentSnapshot`, so later\nsession configuration updates affect future turns without rewriting an\nactive turn.\n- Reuse the service-owned environment manager and resolved snapshot for\nstartup work, MCP initialization, and child-thread spawning instead of\nflowing resolved environments through spawn arguments.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-core --tests`\n- `just test -p codex-core environment_selection`\n- `just test -p codex-core turn_environments`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsession_update_settings_does_not_rewrite_sticky_environment_cwds`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndefault_turn_does_not_overlay_legacy_fallback_cwd_onto_stored_thread_environments`","verified_at":"2026-06-15T23:15:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9728992fab1aaba5d1ca801f22402b7c8c3e5760","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9728992fab1aaba5d1ca801f22402b7c8c3e5760","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9728992fab1aaba5d1ca801f22402b7c8c3e5760/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4c1c9bf327e33fc18cf64af54bf706101659511d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4c1c9bf327e33fc18cf64af54bf706101659511d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4c1c9bf327e33fc18cf64af54bf706101659511d"}]},{"sha":"4c1c9bf327e33fc18cf64af54bf706101659511d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRjMWM5YmYzMjdlMzNmYzE4Y2Y2NGFmNTRiZjcwNjEwMTY1OTUxMWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jameswt-oai","email":"jameswt@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:09:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:09:43Z"},"message":"[codex] Preserve remote plugin directory order (#28395)\n\n## Summary\n\n- preserve the plugin directory endpoint's response order while merging\ninstalled state\n- append unmatched installed-only plugins afterward when requested\n- add focused coverage for directory order and installed-only placement\n\n## Why\n\nThe remote marketplace merge currently reconstructs plugins through\nordered maps and sets, then sorts the result alphabetically by display\nname. That discards any ordering supplied by the plugin directory\nendpoint before the list reaches Desktop.\n\n## Implementation\n\nDirectory plugin IDs are unique, so the merge now iterates the directory\nvector directly in response order. For each directory plugin, it removes\nmatching installed state from an ID-indexed map and builds the summary.\nAny entries left in the installed map are installed-only plugins and are\nappended when `include_installed_only` is enabled.\n\nThere is no separate rank field, rank map, or final sort. Desktop\ntherefore receives directory order—including any backend ranking—and can\npreserve it within its existing stable UI state tiers.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (225 passed)","tree":{"sha":"f26d2a861b98f5fe8330eee20aaba5ea46de78f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f26d2a861b98f5fe8330eee20aaba5ea46de78f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4c1c9bf327e33fc18cf64af54bf706101659511d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMIY3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqsIQAAz2VG2u2MgA5+/+enRoA9YT\nbMhfsFVQ8ZuAHKVj5iY1f0J4WscRlBNlmWLziaWKwrvR25DUHNxKeRnVNbeDQA3i\n+pSVJdKgsM7FWgvuJBI5xuInDKbggidS9DNd584Pd3VMq0AaB3zSYH9J8M+1NoDP\naoRNoH2KPrfj7G4l3QztNyymTcOOw1LXl4c8L3bBCO5o3kxN3JAnL4mDt1iF00Nr\n21ecbLTGTBfmfRWZ8OuP/SFrrAfNAiLj1TQ20og0492hfvwjWGseD3IZrvMFTk0T\naAL5g/UYKYMOeFmSoRXd3cRr6kmfgTRirahNguFwevWZja8dsy7qYJ2kPX+ZUbam\nphCVuuaOUhK3XiCqe3sFKpQPymQA6uain6WV/gD6DXsJPd3ph/5W6Ar09O+FuhfX\nYh2X8IrPUJkegmCM7akvV4YAIQKpOFPhqBxbfMQJcMKm0Mj2dZsLgSlTQT29vpdN\n4QT+IYCG1cxYOeTSl6oIgTkeNEcxJZCVeBbSzrlVdulbPikpzSdiB57jZ374vSZU\nE+ACYB5i0QIJOxw/fK46h4P1pX+Wcnpp5GDBUL9V9LKwOomae+WIsaex2xEcBLdU\ng54wL+dW1T0kHjCPz3JtlytRnYW9bYcXMaMgaEcgUcaKl/bhBsg6BGz80LZw1xsn\nuflvWeKSs3f23MfQDYXp\n=Otdh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f26d2a861b98f5fe8330eee20aaba5ea46de78f3\nparent db8927a8e2a57891955b5fa5f8cb75a69e816f76\nauthor jameswt-oai <jameswt@openai.com> 1781564983 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781564983 -0700\n\n[codex] Preserve remote plugin directory order (#28395)\n\n## Summary\n\n- preserve the plugin directory endpoint's response order while merging\ninstalled state\n- append unmatched installed-only plugins afterward when requested\n- add focused coverage for directory order and installed-only placement\n\n## Why\n\nThe remote marketplace merge currently reconstructs plugins through\nordered maps and sets, then sorts the result alphabetically by display\nname. That discards any ordering supplied by the plugin directory\nendpoint before the list reaches Desktop.\n\n## Implementation\n\nDirectory plugin IDs are unique, so the merge now iterates the directory\nvector directly in response order. For each directory plugin, it removes\nmatching installed state from an ID-indexed map and builds the summary.\nAny entries left in the installed map are installed-only plugins and are\nappended when `include_installed_only` is enabled.\n\nThere is no separate rank field, rank map, or final sort. Desktop\ntherefore receives directory order—including any backend ranking—and can\npreserve it within its existing stable UI state tiers.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (225 passed)","verified_at":"2026-06-15T23:09:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4c1c9bf327e33fc18cf64af54bf706101659511d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4c1c9bf327e33fc18cf64af54bf706101659511d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4c1c9bf327e33fc18cf64af54bf706101659511d/comments","author":{"login":"jameswt-oai","id":247462917,"node_id":"U_kgDODr_8BQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247462917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jameswt-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"db8927a8e2a57891955b5fa5f8cb75a69e816f76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db8927a8e2a57891955b5fa5f8cb75a69e816f76","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/db8927a8e2a57891955b5fa5f8cb75a69e816f76"}]},{"sha":"db8927a8e2a57891955b5fa5f8cb75a69e816f76","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRiODkyN2E4ZTJhNTc4OTE5NTViNWZhNWY4Y2I3NWE2OWU4MTZmNzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"felixxia-oai","email":"felixxia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T22:50:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T22:50:11Z"},"message":"Deflake realtime handoff steering test (#28300)\n\n## Summary\n- keep the realtime mock websocket open for the handoff steering test\nafter scripted responses\n- avoid racing the mock server close before the standalone handoff\nappend is observed, which was showing up as a Windows timeout in CI\n\n__Details__:\nFailures in samples seem to be caused by:\n1. The mock websocket sends conversation.handoff.requested.\n2. The mock immediately closes the websocket because\nstart_websocket_server(...) defaults to close_after_requests: true.\n3. On Windows, that close often surfaces as os error 10053 / 10054.\n4. The realtime stream shuts down before the routed handoff finishes\ncreating/steering the follow-up request.\n5. The test waits for the expected follow-up event and times out.\n\nThe PR changes only step 2: for this test, the mock websocket stays open\nafter sending the scripted handoff event. The same handoff event is\nstill sent, and the test still asserts the important steering behavior:\n1. first Responses request has the original prompt\n2. first request does not contain realtime delegation\n3. second Responses request does contain the realtime delegation\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core --test all\nsuite::realtime_conversation::inbound_handoff_request_steers_active_turn`\n\n## Recent CI failures with the same signature\n\n-\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27538033492/job/81392362858\n  - 2026-06-15, `[codex] update multi-agent v2 prompts`\n- same test failed after `conversation.handoff.requested`; websocket\nread failed with `os error 10053`\n\n-\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27543877820/job/81412200651\n- 2026-06-15, `feat: dispatch queued user messages through core idle\nextensions`\n  - same test failed; websocket read failed with `os error 10054`\n\n-\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27544342375/job/81413801641\n  - 2026-06-15, `[codex] Make marketplace loading capability aware`\n  - same test failed; websocket read failed with `os error 10053`","tree":{"sha":"a7a7f325b58cd668c52d30523da00887a42305dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a7a7f325b58cd668c52d30523da00887a42305dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/db8927a8e2a57891955b5fa5f8cb75a69e816f76","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMIGjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApJwQAFj0VRR3pmmaXiDJRop230RN\nA8XmLFANMwFozgF8lb2W165uM+AxPkm0dFxvJD0HXwcd9pHTsLwPCu8mugVSBSl5\noknjBzDi82DeFSiaTopDaZLawekOAbMaLoOxPjQtUAZe3EkDsk7uLDti1dakMwDw\nZ5Ldl3FcPV1UaZQALUcZiJ9GK61VSMoA0wxBq83bJeLGLq5dVzKQvuMzhAHixAn3\nuYuJf0ep5733ALbPsvcs08eBYDpF7whIFDwFDpOCmhhHwY2OqfTfH8TlQH5Eg8VI\nBe1+LepgX2su48u7WxQi3URfAWmn06ZlodnCtslPxyBJQ5SirrCA/NbFjbgbxc+B\nx+2Q2KXpscYJRM7J3D/XcgBNdsk48Y2BYD5KDc2vBhCKmuUph9lJ7MVmcJ2gRxDW\nLxuu6R8shfZQsTD21BSw16e/t5iS0WNswaTr7gnHoAFArk+A5TOREQeCalV67Ntz\nuCZuKBnHGP4Q3dKo+ND1lL850vSWzmqDLguA+3XdrFLjucnftW/8OSXRL23MVGc4\nYgtrpO0EteNauKoAJkuRmtf03K4yD8D7tcdRxLAklImezoGw92Fi0oYty/GgmYL5\nryH11b5TX6dY4XYUPTIGluc7W4giJ/JXlWSydQouW0Ixyz3YO5jas6m3/9SptCaW\nBmEun0kMh6ju1UKJx9+R\n=jv22\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a7a7f325b58cd668c52d30523da00887a42305dd\nparent 1fbaac1e50bb45e2ba069b872eee1c89dcd47532\nauthor felixxia-oai <felixxia@openai.com> 1781563811 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781563811 +0100\n\nDeflake realtime handoff steering test (#28300)\n\n## Summary\n- keep the realtime mock websocket open for the handoff steering test\nafter scripted responses\n- avoid racing the mock server close before the standalone handoff\nappend is observed, which was showing up as a Windows timeout in CI\n\n__Details__:\nFailures in samples seem to be caused by:\n1. The mock websocket sends conversation.handoff.requested.\n2. The mock immediately closes the websocket because\nstart_websocket_server(...) defaults to close_after_requests: true.\n3. On Windows, that close often surfaces as os error 10053 / 10054.\n4. The realtime stream shuts down before the routed handoff finishes\ncreating/steering the follow-up request.\n5. The test waits for the expected follow-up event and times out.\n\nThe PR changes only step 2: for this test, the mock websocket stays open\nafter sending the scripted handoff event. The same handoff event is\nstill sent, and the test still asserts the important steering behavior:\n1. first Responses request has the original prompt\n2. first request does not contain realtime delegation\n3. second Responses request does contain the realtime delegation\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core --test all\nsuite::realtime_conversation::inbound_handoff_request_steers_active_turn`\n\n## Recent CI failures with the same signature\n\n-\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27538033492/job/81392362858\n  - 2026-06-15, `[codex] update multi-agent v2 prompts`\n- same test failed after `conversation.handoff.requested`; websocket\nread failed with `os error 10053`\n\n-\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27543877820/job/81412200651\n- 2026-06-15, `feat: dispatch queued user messages through core idle\nextensions`\n  - same test failed; websocket read failed with `os error 10054`\n\n-\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27544342375/job/81413801641\n  - 2026-06-15, `[codex] Make marketplace loading capability aware`\n  - same test failed; websocket read failed with `os error 10053`","verified_at":"2026-06-15T22:50:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db8927a8e2a57891955b5fa5f8cb75a69e816f76","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/db8927a8e2a57891955b5fa5f8cb75a69e816f76","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db8927a8e2a57891955b5fa5f8cb75a69e816f76/comments","author":{"login":"felixxia-oai","id":288149840,"node_id":"U_kgDOESzRUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288149840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1fbaac1e50bb45e2ba069b872eee1c89dcd47532","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1fbaac1e50bb45e2ba069b872eee1c89dcd47532","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1fbaac1e50bb45e2ba069b872eee1c89dcd47532"}]},{"sha":"1fbaac1e50bb45e2ba069b872eee1c89dcd47532","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFmYmFhYzFlNTBiYjQ1ZTJiYTA2OWI4NzJlZWUxYzg5ZGNkNDc1MzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Matthew Zeng","email":"mzeng@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T22:24:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T22:24:33Z"},"message":"[codex] Reuse Apps policy evaluation across MCP tool exposure (#27813)\n\n## Summary\n\n- move `AppToolPolicyEvaluator` and the Apps config/requirements policy\nlogic from `codex-core` into `codex-connectors`\n- resolve one immutable policy snapshot per exposure build and reuse it\nacross every Codex Apps MCP tool\n- keep core as a thin adapter from MCP metadata to connector-owned\npolicy input while preserving the call-time defense-in-depth check\n\n## Why\n\n`build_mcp_tool_exposure` evaluates every Codex Apps tool on each\nsampling request. The old path rebuilt effective Apps configuration for\nevery tool, and the policy implementation lived in the already-large\ncore crate even though it is connector-specific.\n\nThe connector-owned evaluator keeps the expensive config merge/decode\nout of the loop and gives core only the effective policy result it\nneeds.\n\n## Performance\n\nWith the real 557-tool Apps corpus, `build_mcp_tool_exposure` measured\n3.74 ms and 3.33 ms after the extraction (3.54 ms mean). The original\npath measured 807 ms mean, so the final result retains the 99.6%\nreduction.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-connectors -p codex-core`\n- `just test -p codex-connectors` — 15 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core --lib connectors` — 35 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core --lib mcp_tool_exposure` — 5 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core --lib mcp_tool_call` — 72 passed\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just fix -p codex-connectors`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"b1860b919cb7d403a8daaa5a4fafe9b47bdd9a0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b1860b919cb7d403a8daaa5a4fafe9b47bdd9a0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1fbaac1e50bb45e2ba069b872eee1c89dcd47532","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMHuhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARSYQAKqtkKL+pDxMWyIAPB6nkE8y\nky9tQZluDlsuHRRZnZgtMSvs0i7WBmKOG/Sb1WN6ym7Eg+lOE4orftgWrvJGJEqv\nEJqSmnA/hccLU3T/keemFK0EinfgcH/gT6krRgg9sQ6ryh/sAKKxOvY0ids/Yvfx\npET9W88aWD6sRyRG01xEeNGui2y1f/RFYcnzn26mPbfFDtw8gIH2CL8ipul+cXBh\npprONeOUg4rzVQ1j2NKVvcQWQ1gWDfX6z3EDHITPQvCU9xldU4k52UV6TMEHFYEo\niJ/JX85YzzqyweRZu7m6G1HuDZvPaA8ir97kfiyenjRiFVLcA6lrVrvpwkoedYF9\naKAXhpa6HuXVtvaqfa3cNwlauiA6Fe3XQ6D09OOuC4ZbqEQla95VpIbhidhGBxej\nLqB4rcy7DfhefLhrY3oMNTRTkmosDz8mq8RMm/s+UJIuYcPJIX48KzvOEB905LKH\nA1nCOJj5mS/uy7xtgnLpSopGn2J/YDQ+OWv3sIIW17ltY+ZqruiGPv38H4596ojm\noi1j37aEnN+7GE/GvlU2nmnhd8vfGwvm3p/7Pz1MzgHzYtMy5R0LB9EydQVNYk83\nekzrOot9M9Wc1emMHM1nrz4aaHvfAFWnt3S35RlyQqX0DeJ93eFnm+T5KcfoPSpu\nFw2HT+hbmMYOrPnGbJdt\n=mhku\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b1860b919cb7d403a8daaa5a4fafe9b47bdd9a0e\nparent d7f298fe20a560fc5bfab78ef19e0c76b4d201bb\nauthor Matthew Zeng <mzeng@openai.com> 1781562273 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781562273 -0700\n\n[codex] Reuse Apps policy evaluation across MCP tool exposure (#27813)\n\n## Summary\n\n- move `AppToolPolicyEvaluator` and the Apps config/requirements policy\nlogic from `codex-core` into `codex-connectors`\n- resolve one immutable policy snapshot per exposure build and reuse it\nacross every Codex Apps MCP tool\n- keep core as a thin adapter from MCP metadata to connector-owned\npolicy input while preserving the call-time defense-in-depth check\n\n## Why\n\n`build_mcp_tool_exposure` evaluates every Codex Apps tool on each\nsampling request. The old path rebuilt effective Apps configuration for\nevery tool, and the policy implementation lived in the already-large\ncore crate even though it is connector-specific.\n\nThe connector-owned evaluator keeps the expensive config merge/decode\nout of the loop and gives core only the effective policy result it\nneeds.\n\n## Performance\n\nWith the real 557-tool Apps corpus, `build_mcp_tool_exposure` measured\n3.74 ms and 3.33 ms after the extraction (3.54 ms mean). The original\npath measured 807 ms mean, so the final result retains the 99.6%\nreduction.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-connectors -p codex-core`\n- `just test -p codex-connectors` — 15 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core --lib connectors` — 35 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core --lib mcp_tool_exposure` — 5 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core --lib mcp_tool_call` — 72 passed\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just fix -p codex-connectors`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-15T22:24:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1fbaac1e50bb45e2ba069b872eee1c89dcd47532","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1fbaac1e50bb45e2ba069b872eee1c89dcd47532","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1fbaac1e50bb45e2ba069b872eee1c89dcd47532/comments","author":{"login":"mzeng-openai","id":175741029,"node_id":"U_kgDOCnmYZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175741029?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/mzeng-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d7f298fe20a560fc5bfab78ef19e0c76b4d201bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d7f298fe20a560fc5bfab78ef19e0c76b4d201bb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d7f298fe20a560fc5bfab78ef19e0c76b4d201bb"}]},{"sha":"d7f298fe20a560fc5bfab78ef19e0c76b4d201bb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ3ZjI5OGZlMjBhNTYwZmM1YmZhYjc4ZWYxOWUwYzc2YjRkMjAxYmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Abhinav","email":"abhinav@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T22:12:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T22:12:26Z"},"message":"Respect blocking PostToolUse hooks in code mode (#28365)\n\n## Summary\n\nMake blocking hook behavior reliable for tools invoked from code mode.\n\nPreviously, a `PostToolUse` hook could block a completed tool result,\nbut code mode would still return the original typed result to\nJavaScript. The hook appeared blocked in hook telemetry while the\nrunning script continued with the result.\n\nThis change:\n\n- rejects the nested JavaScript tool promise when `PostToolUse` blocks\n- normalizes `decision: \"block\"` and exit code 2 to the same blocking\nbehavior\n- surfaces the hook feedback as the rejected promise's error\n- adds end-to-end coverage for the relevant PreToolUse and PostToolUse\ninteractions\n\n## Hook semantics in code mode\n\n| Hook behavior | Code-mode result |\n|---|---|\n| PreToolUse block | Reject the promise before the tool executes |\n| PreToolUse `updatedInput` | Execute the rewritten invocation and\nreturn its result |\n| PostToolUse `decision: \"block\"` | Execute the tool, then reject the\npromise with the hook reason |\n| PostToolUse exit code 2 | Same behavior as `decision: \"block\"` |\n| PostToolUse `continue: false` | Preserve the existing feedback-only\nbehavior; do not reject the promise |\n\n## Test coverage\n\nAdded or strengthened end-to-end coverage proving that:\n\n- a PreToolUse block rejects the JavaScript promise before execution\n- a PreToolUse input rewrite executes only the rewritten command\n- JavaScript receives the rewritten command's result\n- PostToolUse `decision: \"block\"` rejects after the command executes\n- PostToolUse exit code 2 has the same behavior\n- the hook observes the original completed tool response\n- the blocked original result does not reach JavaScript\n- existing direct-mode replacement behavior remains intact\n- `continue: false` without a reason produces deterministic fallback\nfeedback","tree":{"sha":"973438c13f953f63259337f8a12afddc4d592afe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/973438c13f953f63259337f8a12afddc4d592afe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d7f298fe20a560fc5bfab78ef19e0c76b4d201bb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMHjKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUvcQAIVZHqS36WT/ej5E53VKNkM8\nfGWlAuGrB5kcOxM/x+bqPG4FK94ytZP+XrjCfEUqSCHD8mlgkDAzLSeiETA5XsxB\nIAzpX6jiVxOPTF5PE5hk/JdjsXewWK3RSFH7jN9GcLFeOCGVRXi9+yLB+7VeE/4u\nEWHd1M1D+aDhr8kS25iKavjUZrPlAkaG1ht+P6A61WONlHcVvVPga8Zpz1ECKw2G\nBe1GxdFayCU49Xl6WK4xzFEqmi41OUvoyyA6Gnlx52RFbsJpUybzaBR9/zxPAXWK\nFQ0tonwD6UB7Xa4AiYD5wBYmWNmfRzZxA36T7Q6mA4cAZgrtKCpbk/4G15XKIeSh\n4ktckUnQHKqqGyQ/F1IP3HlxcEqqfiLDdhlmeF/+3N3ZtAIEWsc+P7TgrTqVVAHb\n8eLj8+akQB+gqAN68a+/tdAAsVZa8sntM/9UmMIv1yboAAwWG+B+0eqUeteJr9Fl\nAeOZlC8RdgJwqn0ppNEPfL879OAlIi23ArAhMrmRVskrzEbYNcilqGy5nC9Bz6LG\nbyIOu1o7zo5YmA7b87OMtcR3B7qtid+LS2j/6u/zJDkJZoIfnkpTqew7t2mw0AhX\nHHMYt94dSt/8ufr0sywGtq3/I9aRwzbVaG0DnMjHje1ViG0eMk4qn6M1OWzVgSRc\nOStM+BDMTkNej9B1/OL0\n=xQqN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 973438c13f953f63259337f8a12afddc4d592afe\nparent 709f19e1114583fc891fbba7c705af90f51d9d71\nauthor Abhinav <abhinav@openai.com> 1781561546 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781561546 -0700\n\nRespect blocking PostToolUse hooks in code mode (#28365)\n\n## Summary\n\nMake blocking hook behavior reliable for tools invoked from code mode.\n\nPreviously, a `PostToolUse` hook could block a completed tool result,\nbut code mode would still return the original typed result to\nJavaScript. The hook appeared blocked in hook telemetry while the\nrunning script continued with the result.\n\nThis change:\n\n- rejects the nested JavaScript tool promise when `PostToolUse` blocks\n- normalizes `decision: \"block\"` and exit code 2 to the same blocking\nbehavior\n- surfaces the hook feedback as the rejected promise's error\n- adds end-to-end coverage for the relevant PreToolUse and PostToolUse\ninteractions\n\n## Hook semantics in code mode\n\n| Hook behavior | Code-mode result |\n|---|---|\n| PreToolUse block | Reject the promise before the tool executes |\n| PreToolUse `updatedInput` | Execute the rewritten invocation and\nreturn its result |\n| PostToolUse `decision: \"block\"` | Execute the tool, then reject the\npromise with the hook reason |\n| PostToolUse exit code 2 | Same behavior as `decision: \"block\"` |\n| PostToolUse `continue: false` | Preserve the existing feedback-only\nbehavior; do not reject the promise |\n\n## Test coverage\n\nAdded or strengthened end-to-end coverage proving that:\n\n- a PreToolUse block rejects the JavaScript promise before execution\n- a PreToolUse input rewrite executes only the rewritten command\n- JavaScript receives the rewritten command's result\n- PostToolUse `decision: \"block\"` rejects after the command executes\n- PostToolUse exit code 2 has the same behavior\n- the hook observes the original completed tool response\n- the blocked original result does not reach JavaScript\n- existing direct-mode replacement behavior remains intact\n- `continue: false` without a reason produces deterministic fallback\nfeedback","verified_at":"2026-06-15T22:12:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d7f298fe20a560fc5bfab78ef19e0c76b4d201bb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d7f298fe20a560fc5bfab78ef19e0c76b4d201bb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d7f298fe20a560fc5bfab78ef19e0c76b4d201bb/comments","author":{"login":"abhinav-oai","id":274334565,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFoDZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274334565?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/abhinav-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"709f19e1114583fc891fbba7c705af90f51d9d71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/709f19e1114583fc891fbba7c705af90f51d9d71","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/709f19e1114583fc891fbba7c705af90f51d9d71"}]},{"sha":"709f19e1114583fc891fbba7c705af90f51d9d71","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDcwOWYxOWUxMTE0NTgzZmM4OTFmYmJhN2M3MDVhZjkwZjUxZDlkNzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Ning","email":"ericning@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T22:07:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T22:07:07Z"},"message":"[codex] Add created-by-me remote plugin marketplace (#28203)\n\n## Summary\n- add the `created-by-me-remote` marketplace backed by paginated\n`scope=USER` plugin directory and installed-plugin requests\n- include USER plugins in installed-plugin caching, bundle sync, and\nstale-cache cleanup without client-side discoverability filtering\n- expose the marketplace through app-server v2 and regenerate the\nprotocol schemas\n\n## Testing\n- `cargo build -p codex-app-server --bin codex-app-server`\n- production-auth `plugin/list` smoke test for `created-by-me-remote`\n(returned the expected USER plugin as installed and enabled)\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (221 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol` (231 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server suite::v2::plugin_list::` (37 passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-core-plugins -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"3e1e5cdb42cdf51b7566de841ce3fc5718330b5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3e1e5cdb42cdf51b7566de841ce3fc5718330b5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/709f19e1114583fc891fbba7c705af90f51d9d71","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMHeLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfnAQAK7dmjGB+cDt1iI0GFjE5yNX\nntvhZUSGKaqfe5oJGaq+HsHPVKih3tI2S52tgNZ0bnYsU0CY7o/6YJmjtCuncdlp\nTbqgXMSuCTrH+owwhfqI+fUlXjSaUjLSbjj0g3+3VXX1kGztBwP361H/cRqLc2PQ\nMf42iuZs0kjM437zslNK6DWjMvWoCQ06sVX9QhbDJoKtiw3voQtZnqWsyStMccyA\n/UE3BqSKbEr4qqFuWy6EFPj/RzG1Uq7+SD/7M/L7rGmnU97BwRmOeGf9u5ze8Y4/\nsaEuEiZDJoonHgKsWjUsPLU0F0w3nZCm6QNqHdo+ufRqrb6Gz1kVqUN0GcUlk+RA\n85W70MJiIf+DCJ2plJ7hQKUfEOg3+a89C3Nn57NjulmD/IXWPpUazWJ3Z5Bnh9Sr\nNDkx00n1yOwmTcDVPqHOozgBldwzmpDDSqWxVEKMKArqQpLTAJyIJcwTdhMFlNGQ\n3nyEf2RiaCkNWuzmu6IohkdMk53cirq6vRXKUoxSLNvkbcKrROX1D/dPoCaFPwkb\n9hx9L4calJ/SeBqjje782DuQSvdsP7wM2Q/SNOOcnbhaZDkSYNgtRb7p8VmV2syn\ntOWi9wHjJ1FbbH3TSZXVatO8sFjBEa4nCW17ICoZqn+ia/X87uc6cgZAYR2I6mA9\n2vXEsnV+oYtiGm4Otmwd\n=/CRP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3e1e5cdb42cdf51b7566de841ce3fc5718330b5d\nparent 040dafa32d5312f7803786d208ed6a0a11dfdabb\nauthor Eric Ning <ericning@openai.com> 1781561227 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781561227 +0000\n\n[codex] Add created-by-me remote plugin marketplace (#28203)\n\n## Summary\n- add the `created-by-me-remote` marketplace backed by paginated\n`scope=USER` plugin directory and installed-plugin requests\n- include USER plugins in installed-plugin caching, bundle sync, and\nstale-cache cleanup without client-side discoverability filtering\n- expose the marketplace through app-server v2 and regenerate the\nprotocol schemas\n\n## Testing\n- `cargo build -p codex-app-server --bin codex-app-server`\n- production-auth `plugin/list` smoke test for `created-by-me-remote`\n(returned the expected USER plugin as installed and enabled)\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (221 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol` (231 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server suite::v2::plugin_list::` (37 passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-core-plugins -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-15T22:07:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/709f19e1114583fc891fbba7c705af90f51d9d71","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/709f19e1114583fc891fbba7c705af90f51d9d71","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/709f19e1114583fc891fbba7c705af90f51d9d71/comments","author":{"login":"ericning-o","id":182030612,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtmRFA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182030612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o","html_url":"https://github.com/ericning-o","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"040dafa32d5312f7803786d208ed6a0a11dfdabb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/040dafa32d5312f7803786d208ed6a0a11dfdabb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/040dafa32d5312f7803786d208ed6a0a11dfdabb"}]},{"sha":"040dafa32d5312f7803786d208ed6a0a11dfdabb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDA0MGRhZmEzMmQ1MzEyZjc4MDM3ODZkMjA4ZWQ2YTBhMTFkZmRhYmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-06-15T22:05:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T22:05:28Z"},"message":"feat(core): add metadata field to ResponseItem (#28355)\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR adds an optional `metadata` field to `ResponseItem` for\nResponses API calls. Only mechanical plumbing, no actual values\npopulated and sent yet. Turns out just adding a new field to\n`ResponseItem` has quite a large blast radius already.\n\nThis change is backwards compatible because `metadata` is optional and\nomitted when absent, so existing response items and rollout history\nwithout it still deserialize and requests that do not set it keep the\nsame wire shape. For provider compatibility, we strip out `metadata`\nbefore non-OpenAI Responses requests so Azure and AWS Bedrock never see\nthis field.\n\nMy followup PR here will actually make use of it to start storing and\npassing along `turn_id`: https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/28360\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `ResponseItemMetadata` with optional `turn_id`, plus optional\n`metadata` on Responses API item variants and inter-agent communication.\n- Preserved item metadata through response-item rewrites such as\ntruncation, missing tool-output synthesis, compaction history\nrebuilding, visible-history conversion, rollout/resume, and generated\napp-server schemas/types.\n- Strip item metadata from non-OpenAI Responses requests while\npreserving it for OpenAI-shaped requests.\n- Updated the mechanical fixture/test construction churn required by the\nnew optional field.","tree":{"sha":"506bf32e32bacab8654d401461abb5c747edb1c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/506bf32e32bacab8654d401461abb5c747edb1c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/040dafa32d5312f7803786d208ed6a0a11dfdabb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMHcoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2XIQAGFMESOb4kRrh0pAkHVxh03O\nIBdB1GsBGkc0uClR/m/vCtsixaLa+NZgW0jtGHW0PxaiWBMJBUX5Byglw/1zUP/L\nu4M+vAUrcUJ7kFwz6T1Sxx6j6ZzWqVrIEkhxG3hFkVtl4+vJKMCT8ZijDJvCBsvB\n59JAkNVyQcm9JV2pjxoDqk9uv+RMhI6TyqWmD27fIm6QnzvMeYZY+Zw9ojyvQngv\nORUgboQfkCklHH0ScQcZs/uWtzSttikXCZ1hdVKgPw9JbjabpxSlErpoaXBrna+c\nev1iCas8hqs+G3B8k/oYl5EXjVLYn8i3kyeq2DcCcsCGDztIVQjf5R6oJ+evSXgN\nu8Y0XETyeSvD6+ndmXkaKZT10lKRD2pi06U20W6iDXiE0dpAdaG1gI4YR2UlwYD2\nDzJL6U3e1S0sPn8S2GTCFM/0EJzz/dHRWl7sLY7doBGEU3eA1tJqQno4I0XGbBoo\n/YXj2NWJfbe2ceM3sxLB2snU1JAEH/f1pMn5BsxpIOkDHQQihpGzaJRjfuvI+lUA\nHjFC+a0rUtMtrHChJCJ3kYAGMKxChjDVdYRed9yn6YxQrDlBgTQTg5vXdInY+8Iq\nNlwMPwl46WePD2dV61aymDXoYp+inhmHIx7zcY5JytTAk/9lSkenHSH3NXWBxnUa\navTv8sHdq0uGpEQXqHJx\n=ADdq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 506bf32e32bacab8654d401461abb5c747edb1c9\nparent bef99f861b365377caa9c095f20a8adf4eae4647\nauthor Owen Lin <owenlin0@gmail.com> 1781561128 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781561128 -0700\n\nfeat(core): add metadata field to ResponseItem (#28355)\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR adds an optional `metadata` field to `ResponseItem` for\nResponses API calls. Only mechanical plumbing, no actual values\npopulated and sent yet. Turns out just adding a new field to\n`ResponseItem` has quite a large blast radius already.\n\nThis change is backwards compatible because `metadata` is optional and\nomitted when absent, so existing response items and rollout history\nwithout it still deserialize and requests that do not set it keep the\nsame wire shape. For provider compatibility, we strip out `metadata`\nbefore non-OpenAI Responses requests so Azure and AWS Bedrock never see\nthis field.\n\nMy followup PR here will actually make use of it to start storing and\npassing along `turn_id`: https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/28360\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `ResponseItemMetadata` with optional `turn_id`, plus optional\n`metadata` on Responses API item variants and inter-agent communication.\n- Preserved item metadata through response-item rewrites such as\ntruncation, missing tool-output synthesis, compaction history\nrebuilding, visible-history conversion, rollout/resume, and generated\napp-server schemas/types.\n- Strip item metadata from non-OpenAI Responses requests while\npreserving it for OpenAI-shaped requests.\n- Updated the mechanical fixture/test construction churn required by the\nnew optional field.","verified_at":"2026-06-15T22:05:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/040dafa32d5312f7803786d208ed6a0a11dfdabb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/040dafa32d5312f7803786d208ed6a0a11dfdabb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/040dafa32d5312f7803786d208ed6a0a11dfdabb/comments","author":{"login":"owenlin0","id":947871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0Nzg3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/947871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0","html_url":"https://github.com/owenlin0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bef99f861b365377caa9c095f20a8adf4eae4647","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bef99f861b365377caa9c095f20a8adf4eae4647","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bef99f861b365377caa9c095f20a8adf4eae4647"}]},{"sha":"bef99f861b365377caa9c095f20a8adf4eae4647","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJlZjk5Zjg2MWIzNjUzNzdjYWE5YzA5NWYyMGE4YWRmNGVhZTQ2NDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"jay","email":"jayp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T21:54:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T21:54:01Z"},"message":"feat(app-server): expose rate-limit reset credits (#28143)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex users can earn personal rate-limit reset credits, but app-server\nclients do not currently have an API for reading or redeeming them. This\nadds the backend and protocol foundation used by the `/usage` TUI flow\nin #28154.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Extend `account/rateLimits/read` with a nullable\n`rateLimitResetCredits` summary sourced from the existing usage\nresponse.\n- Add backend-client and app-server support for consuming a reset with a\ncaller-generated idempotency key. A UUID is recommended, and clients\nreuse the same key when retrying the same logical reset.\n- Return only the consume `outcome`; clients refetch\n`account/rateLimits/read` for updated window state.\n- Document the response field and each consume outcome, and regenerate\nthe JSON and TypeScript schema fixtures.\n- Clarify in `AGENTS.md` that new app-server string enum values use\ncamelCase on the wire.\n- Update the existing TUI response fixture for the expanded protocol\nshape.\n- Add coverage for authentication, response mapping, backend failures,\nconsume outcomes, and request timeout behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol` — 231 passed.\n- `just test -p codex-backend-client` — 14 passed.\n- Focused `codex-app-server` reset-credit tests — 5 passed.\n- Focused `codex-tui` protocol response fixture test — passed.\n- `just fix -p codex-backend-client -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server` — passed.\n- `just fmt` — passed.","tree":{"sha":"677013dff54a33d17ddbd0330bfd9f0b5b59c338","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/677013dff54a33d17ddbd0330bfd9f0b5b59c338"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bef99f861b365377caa9c095f20a8adf4eae4647","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMHR5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+D8QACK9NPs+kdWLR+NS/HIFZNcJ\nzD5ogKQxCR4Yw1H4/6y4FGkLBuWtwx1FCkh5StpAJOJp3l+7K9EQPGhWZa9Hl8sb\nqhOwAAOQzCLxRak+Fp27m8oXvV9rdaslPNZNM12T9uO2z9d84ziHK/rEdsekkpv4\n9AlWKV2pEd8VWFCiwY074Vz80jgTnW5rOrgg62yLSKwzBPfjlgMZkUP6UlrkZGb5\npk7dD7NJHTD21ewXpK346bMqISbvM0sgHoMwGiMxGksvU7YU5DfQupeLAOhl74/R\nOjz5iW2dt60fRB9TVw1uzpXDp2ITQsVDzGFWwnAeTpTg8tSu7brG/PFieT4dnU2v\nDRsjgZUjXP0ZLGiBaIExgqyYr1jRdzm2mUJJ64DZDsk0IgiUXo4u9+pj2eu/9lm0\nrSdoOw4MT1UDuw8zMRcqw2FE+80pFw8i2qk3bsqDw3M/jp73+4eox9OeN30VhCxe\nnUCuQe98kSFKSeqpFBdODAbigEzvR/bsocMYaG9wEjRB90k+5yIZDEfgUZCugrEN\n0k/RLZMp+PVkIj2oFydmvEBm4RAEJQYSoXlKSA6UcB3Z6YrbCEla2u4zrfCpU6AR\nDWy+vxwMh4XQ7tUF0xacMFuTn3fArxdR4zIkV/dRd7uCY3Xn6g+41Cz9Y9hvbUrU\nBSxCjYPXmTkEzp+eJLfG\n=Osl/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 677013dff54a33d17ddbd0330bfd9f0b5b59c338\nparent af99f6a72fe7369f327cec90718052b7da3d633a\nauthor jay <jayp@openai.com> 1781560441 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781560441 +0000\n\nfeat(app-server): expose rate-limit reset credits (#28143)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex users can earn personal rate-limit reset credits, but app-server\nclients do not currently have an API for reading or redeeming them. This\nadds the backend and protocol foundation used by the `/usage` TUI flow\nin #28154.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Extend `account/rateLimits/read` with a nullable\n`rateLimitResetCredits` summary sourced from the existing usage\nresponse.\n- Add backend-client and app-server support for consuming a reset with a\ncaller-generated idempotency key. A UUID is recommended, and clients\nreuse the same key when retrying the same logical reset.\n- Return only the consume `outcome`; clients refetch\n`account/rateLimits/read` for updated window state.\n- Document the response field and each consume outcome, and regenerate\nthe JSON and TypeScript schema fixtures.\n- Clarify in `AGENTS.md` that new app-server string enum values use\ncamelCase on the wire.\n- Update the existing TUI response fixture for the expanded protocol\nshape.\n- Add coverage for authentication, response mapping, backend failures,\nconsume outcomes, and request timeout behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol` — 231 passed.\n- `just test -p codex-backend-client` — 14 passed.\n- Focused `codex-app-server` reset-credit tests — 5 passed.\n- Focused `codex-tui` protocol response fixture test — passed.\n- `just fix -p codex-backend-client -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server` — passed.\n- `just fmt` — passed.","verified_at":"2026-06-15T21:54:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bef99f861b365377caa9c095f20a8adf4eae4647","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bef99f861b365377caa9c095f20a8adf4eae4647","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bef99f861b365377caa9c095f20a8adf4eae4647/comments","author":{"login":"jayp-oai","id":286152634,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5Xug","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286152634?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jayp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"af99f6a72fe7369f327cec90718052b7da3d633a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/af99f6a72fe7369f327cec90718052b7da3d633a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/af99f6a72fe7369f327cec90718052b7da3d633a"}]},{"sha":"af99f6a72fe7369f327cec90718052b7da3d633a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFmOTlmNmE3MmZlNzM2OWYzMjdjZWM5MDcxODA1MmI3ZGEzZDYzM2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"mchen-oai","email":"mchen@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T21:48:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T21:48:30Z"},"message":"core: cache the tool search handler per session (#27258)\n\n## Why\n\nTool router construction rebuilds the deferred-tool BM25 index during\nsession initialization and before each sampling continuation, even when\nthe searchable tool metadata is unchanged. Local profiling measured\n`append_tool_search_executor` at roughly 113 ms per continuation, making\nrepeated index construction the largest measured router-building cost.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a session-scoped `ToolSearchHandlerCache` so continuations and\nuser turns can reuse the existing handler.\n- Key reuse on the complete ordered `Vec<ToolSearchInfo>`, rebuilding\nwhen searchable text, loadable tool specs, source metadata, or ordering\nchanges.\n- Build handlers outside the cache lock and recheck before publishing\nthem, avoiding holding the mutex during index construction.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cache_reuses_identical_search_infos_and_rebuilds_changed_inputs`\ncovers exact cache reuse and invalidation when the ordered search\nmetadata changes.\n- Local rollout profiling showed the initial router build populating the\ncache and unchanged later continuations reusing it:\n  - uncached: 118 ms median across 14 spans from 3 rollouts\n  - cached: 4 ms median across 12 spans from 3 rollouts","tree":{"sha":"4e13acf2b600f211dcb6be2ebe01066de7b81eb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4e13acf2b600f211dcb6be2ebe01066de7b81eb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/af99f6a72fe7369f327cec90718052b7da3d633a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMHMuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQEMQABhs/sOLypC4NgMwlj2NWV8V\n12swGedfKmWFmNGAC34VPdm241J0M14kdtsQWH+EVuHWA9ig46vVBVa7p5MlQo8m\nHz3Fxt0q446b9B0RxKprvY69ZdDX0kj3o3JPrVRqG47f+MXaicmNtqjPEhmGQ05E\njoDPdBnAw3/G+8nDnnlq6vjRGuZklEWcY/YI69MUwZDqesSmqQTY+qoKTJXyIIFx\nGn8NU99kU8uJuS5+uN7MjPLkvnD6HHXrX75Uha4nZcYmPHm5IvUzI7QmS6TFZG/e\nYz1p46PNGb/w+ssfRZUWMCeEwTDhSEfxGPGWvFNYlkIBzF1Mq0hEM2GFoUAFyewE\nDPzPpKoxajgfXB8QIOI62eVrhOLqQZ8psvNed8lJjWREJeTIXVNFuCPqr/ZyxaT6\ntvNa3czYGIkcDMYr3Ugmi6n8hwohE455ESfGBLWMhGsvdSOrLMfKKK9fpgTT0yfI\nMJiOD8xXvOo65k7hbd1hukQASVKD/rPspG+4x3ZEl7OqznU1S3QkE1ynAldeYQnB\nyoEkN2RZb+zPnr7rI3l4WnKug/Zd/ZCI8zQ9LEQQRkKgG+Yf/7L9vExt9VqxptxP\njqaUINoefuMulxCVqWn1TcTU3C+Z/j9cSOmQie2FcuaDdSL+oPRXh/UHJ8vFyEJ6\nVj3DdjxqXKgyVn6qEpPG\n=M7z4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4e13acf2b600f211dcb6be2ebe01066de7b81eb9\nparent fbbe7706d65df02d6d1b7db5ae6f9e50de216da7\nauthor mchen-oai <mchen@openai.com> 1781560110 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781560110 -0700\n\ncore: cache the tool search handler per session (#27258)\n\n## Why\n\nTool router construction rebuilds the deferred-tool BM25 index during\nsession initialization and before each sampling continuation, even when\nthe searchable tool metadata is unchanged. Local profiling measured\n`append_tool_search_executor` at roughly 113 ms per continuation, making\nrepeated index construction the largest measured router-building cost.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a session-scoped `ToolSearchHandlerCache` so continuations and\nuser turns can reuse the existing handler.\n- Key reuse on the complete ordered `Vec<ToolSearchInfo>`, rebuilding\nwhen searchable text, loadable tool specs, source metadata, or ordering\nchanges.\n- Build handlers outside the cache lock and recheck before publishing\nthem, avoiding holding the mutex during index construction.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cache_reuses_identical_search_infos_and_rebuilds_changed_inputs`\ncovers exact cache reuse and invalidation when the ordered search\nmetadata changes.\n- Local rollout profiling showed the initial router build populating the\ncache and unchanged later continuations reusing it:\n  - uncached: 118 ms median across 14 spans from 3 rollouts\n  - cached: 4 ms median across 12 spans from 3 rollouts","verified_at":"2026-06-15T21:48:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/af99f6a72fe7369f327cec90718052b7da3d633a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/af99f6a72fe7369f327cec90718052b7da3d633a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/af99f6a72fe7369f327cec90718052b7da3d633a/comments","author":{"login":"mchen-oai","id":250037145,"node_id":"U_kgDODudDmQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250037145?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mchen-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/mchen-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mchen-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mchen-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mchen-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mchen-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mchen-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mchen-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mchen-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mchen-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mchen-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fbbe7706d65df02d6d1b7db5ae6f9e50de216da7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fbbe7706d65df02d6d1b7db5ae6f9e50de216da7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fbbe7706d65df02d6d1b7db5ae6f9e50de216da7"}]},{"sha":"fbbe7706d65df02d6d1b7db5ae6f9e50de216da7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZiYmU3NzA2ZDY1ZGYwMmQ2ZDFiN2RiNWFlNmY5ZTUwZGUyMTZkYTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T21:30:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T21:30:32Z"},"message":"Add hidden Windows sandbox wrapper entrypoint (#28358)\n\n## Why\n\nThis is the second PR in the Windows fs-helper sandbox stack. The\nfs-helper path needs a Windows sandbox launcher that has the same\nargv-shaped contract as macOS `sandbox-exec` and `codex-linux-sandbox`,\nbut this PR only introduces that hidden launcher. It does not route\nfs-helper through it yet.\n\nThe hidden launcher still needs to be policy-complete before later\ndirect-spawn callers use it. In particular, it has to carry the same\nWindows sandbox policy details that the existing spawn paths already\nunderstand: proxy enforcement, read/write root overrides, and\ndeny-read/deny-write overrides.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added the hidden `codex.exe --run-as-windows-sandbox` arg1 dispatch\npath.\n- Added `windows-sandbox-rs/src/wrapper.rs`, which parses the wrapper\nargv, launches the requested command through the shared Windows sandbox\nsession runner from PR1, and forwards stdio.\n- Added `create_windows_sandbox_command_args_for_permission_profile()`\nso later direct-spawn callers can build the wrapper argv consistently.\n- Made the wrapper argv round-trip the full Windows sandbox policy\nsurface it needs later: workspace roots, environment, permission\nprofile, sandbox level, private desktop, proxy enforcement, read/write\nroot overrides, and deny-read/deny-write overrides.\n- Carried `proxy_enforced` through the shared Windows session request so\nproxy-managed executions continue to use the offline/elevated sandbox\nidentity.\n- Added wrapper argument round-trip coverage for the full policy fields.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox windows_wrapper_args_round_trip`\n- `just test -p codex-arg0`\n- `just test -p codex-core exec::tests::windows_`\n- `just fix -p codex-windows-sandbox -p codex-core -p codex-cli`\n\nLocal note: the full `just fmt` command still fails on this workstation\nin non-Rust formatter setup (`uv` cache access denied and missing\n`dotslash`/buildifier), but the Rust formatter phase completed.","tree":{"sha":"814abb7976e09be08142d0a6842f19056be081a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/814abb7976e09be08142d0a6842f19056be081a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fbbe7706d65df02d6d1b7db5ae6f9e50de216da7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMG74CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOMcQAKj4R/PTZNTHSmvR7+lfqn2L\nZmDjFkteaFlsj6fAgQ5SyAmCFSOmIWpMc9H2FVNsWkhY3mxSg/wvjzqwomfqpl4z\ndg/zlDPhdOHA/T4HcApyh4ABHVM6sVsgSVlplcaaM0MicX4UBTdQP/CiJA0+EYWl\nIs9D4gpkL41GmmBKHo/y1z3HoZiSJyd2IU0TT1sZAblsiriGRRw+x3ZlcTOhjguc\n7PCW4LQfUfMSGQfwC9st93xC1W+ff4vRpTGjeqtPpLLQLM0QCBYrLQYSSseG1Ewy\n/BFLveToq1jIIJBAO6v2J4BlvwQMQnH/ujZJKXRQRPswdfjpPcNH3bWqEJpdpiDL\naJkzAdZjcMzhi4yJL4RGT7k3QwEcw5GEq/cq62NoNjo7H2/Ke6AhLtcHgrimCYFY\nOso2HT9MrDbzxublfPLlmRloAq61zbkjLrsfB5ksM7/lGvm4l4OE55f5Pp/56EYR\nKRz29B+llAtHEkDNjWH8Dr5bgVM2q0SbM0lfgyLqBBgB5yXJgMcHx3KTC/IubvWw\nfBJr0PooJ9S8PoYXV6VexOb8uwszck4sySaFHrDBaUk51ufa00L7oQ3FDbHDleGD\nNqxAuPmQRjbDKuexTKXvR40A7vDpfQxw6cREhTxsXhHMyN2I409e7Zl43RTJIeY7\nntjujiTpdvw7Scv4pG6s\n=BJoq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 814abb7976e09be08142d0a6842f19056be081a1\nparent e7a9988d1abfedf67ecf5ae03ce15ecd0b9d82a1\nauthor iceweasel-oai <iceweasel@openai.com> 1781559032 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781559032 +0000\n\nAdd hidden Windows sandbox wrapper entrypoint (#28358)\n\n## Why\n\nThis is the second PR in the Windows fs-helper sandbox stack. The\nfs-helper path needs a Windows sandbox launcher that has the same\nargv-shaped contract as macOS `sandbox-exec` and `codex-linux-sandbox`,\nbut this PR only introduces that hidden launcher. It does not route\nfs-helper through it yet.\n\nThe hidden launcher still needs to be policy-complete before later\ndirect-spawn callers use it. In particular, it has to carry the same\nWindows sandbox policy details that the existing spawn paths already\nunderstand: proxy enforcement, read/write root overrides, and\ndeny-read/deny-write overrides.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added the hidden `codex.exe --run-as-windows-sandbox` arg1 dispatch\npath.\n- Added `windows-sandbox-rs/src/wrapper.rs`, which parses the wrapper\nargv, launches the requested command through the shared Windows sandbox\nsession runner from PR1, and forwards stdio.\n- Added `create_windows_sandbox_command_args_for_permission_profile()`\nso later direct-spawn callers can build the wrapper argv consistently.\n- Made the wrapper argv round-trip the full Windows sandbox policy\nsurface it needs later: workspace roots, environment, permission\nprofile, sandbox level, private desktop, proxy enforcement, read/write\nroot overrides, and deny-read/deny-write overrides.\n- Carried `proxy_enforced` through the shared Windows session request so\nproxy-managed executions continue to use the offline/elevated sandbox\nidentity.\n- Added wrapper argument round-trip coverage for the full policy fields.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox windows_wrapper_args_round_trip`\n- `just test -p codex-arg0`\n- `just test -p codex-core exec::tests::windows_`\n- `just fix -p codex-windows-sandbox -p codex-core -p codex-cli`\n\nLocal note: the full `just fmt` command still fails on this workstation\nin non-Rust formatter setup (`uv` cache access denied and missing\n`dotslash`/buildifier), but the Rust formatter phase completed.","verified_at":"2026-06-15T21:30:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fbbe7706d65df02d6d1b7db5ae6f9e50de216da7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fbbe7706d65df02d6d1b7db5ae6f9e50de216da7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fbbe7706d65df02d6d1b7db5ae6f9e50de216da7/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e7a9988d1abfedf67ecf5ae03ce15ecd0b9d82a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7a9988d1abfedf67ecf5ae03ce15ecd0b9d82a1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e7a9988d1abfedf67ecf5ae03ce15ecd0b9d82a1"}]},{"sha":"e7a9988d1abfedf67ecf5ae03ce15ecd0b9d82a1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU3YTk5ODhkMWFiZmVkZjY3ZWNmNWFlMDNjZTE1ZWNkMGI5ZDgyYTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T20:56:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T20:56:18Z"},"message":"Add Windows unified exec yield floor (#27086)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Windows `unified_exec` experiment regressed at the turn level in a\nway that points to premature backgrounding / extra command cycles rather\nthan individual responses getting heavier:\n\n- `codex_local_tool_calls_per_turn` was up about 20.7%.\n- `codex_local_blended_tokens_per_turn` was up about 4.1%, and\n`codex_local_output_tokens_per_turn` was up about 4.0%.\n- `codex_local_response_latency_per_turn` was up about 8.3%.\n- The primary activity metrics also moved down: `codex_turns` about\n-6.6%, `codex_dau` about -1.0%, and `codex_local_hourly_active_users`\nabout -3.0%.\n\nAt the same time, the per-response metrics moved in the other direction:\nblended tokens per response, output tokens per response, and latency per\nresponse were all lower in test. That suggests the bad turn-level shape\nis largely about extra tool/model cycles, not each response being slower\nor more expensive on its own.\n\nLocal Windows benchmarking showed the likely mechanism: shell-wrapped\ncommands pay a large PowerShell startup/teardown tax before the actual\ncommand has much time to run. In the benchmark, the PowerShell wrapper\nadded roughly 0.7-1.0s versus direct exec:\n\n- Windows PowerShell: about 740ms p50 / 800ms p90 overhead versus direct\nexec.\n- PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`): about 930ms p50 / 980ms p90 overhead versus\ndirect exec.\n\nThe model commonly asks for a 1s initial yield. On Windows, that can\nspend nearly the whole window waiting on PowerShell machinery, so\notherwise-short commands are more likely to return as background\nsessions and require follow-up polling/tool calls.\n\nThis is intentionally a temporary unlock. It gives Windows closer to the\nsame useful post-shell command window as other platforms while we work\non reducing the PowerShell tax directly, for example with persistent\nPowerShell workers or conservative direct-exec paths for commands that\ndo not need shell semantics.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a Windows-only 2s floor to `unified_exec`'s initial\n`yield_time_ms` clamp.\n- Keeps larger model-requested waits unchanged, including the existing\n10s default.\n- Keeps the existing 30s max clamp.\n- Leaves non-Windows behavior unchanged.\n- Adds platform-gated tests for both the Windows floor and the\nnon-Windows clamp behavior.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core unified_exec`","tree":{"sha":"f613399ea0ea0272d42256d5b58c1cd4ace66106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f613399ea0ea0272d42256d5b58c1cd4ace66106"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e7a9988d1abfedf67ecf5ae03ce15ecd0b9d82a1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMGbyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATlMQAIIEL7YZWAGfb8uC1Nm0Olsb\ngsqIwGI3T73HH7i20mG11teV9QkOY3PFj5KaUB5UuC3Czn40nZyyANjO1dobY57J\nrI4J9XkHX1bZhxuT/ZWC4b2zvBCE7hZukjKzHbyqUHLKKN0ysOeT62We0aMig6Lr\n3Mws+h7tvt8+a4hbAUoeefGTCPi7x9EwaWe5dKNtdGTShtcaPpPhRdrfV5KBb/yS\nw1GYANjX4D0TtN8Y8lBXbENELlLzdhDhubR+aC/0SeTvDCw/kQzaFBhyh+RXx5Br\nex7gsoPmlwa2zi84ZDnuwyMp9q+5gHxUbm6Z1VgvurNwfSYNIaSMiD4qjnm9PpGu\neuXo3KYBexqJmUV+6QKiaap0hra0SOxknuKIobRlcwSEIWwAG2hyxz8M0nWa+xPI\noWfA4mBZ923M7q2HF6NzbZLe63t7vHKcD8gPwuzfBYs/8ugd8fKm+DmRxeIOJJez\nuiykDx225odntkQkMMtvn4qNscei1qOkpTNZhaydaHx7WVKoLNSXtQE3PXliRe4W\njA3Su9XhKlP39PCfK414erXei2isPg3qZ4CSL/ETotjA+lDZak5Q8TT83DFvZCz8\nDYW1w9G3qTiF11F8jx3WAZ/WdbjnmxQ1PccyU6rRtRaH9Cmz1OtM8d5ocf2ZWRxv\nfc8n8FW9eTcNjHErKv5f\n=JY3d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f613399ea0ea0272d42256d5b58c1cd4ace66106\nparent c0b36d234a8cdbd9aa0790f5a8cbf73b7456d915\nauthor iceweasel-oai <iceweasel@openai.com> 1781556978 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781556978 -0700\n\nAdd Windows unified exec yield floor (#27086)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Windows `unified_exec` experiment regressed at the turn level in a\nway that points to premature backgrounding / extra command cycles rather\nthan individual responses getting heavier:\n\n- `codex_local_tool_calls_per_turn` was up about 20.7%.\n- `codex_local_blended_tokens_per_turn` was up about 4.1%, and\n`codex_local_output_tokens_per_turn` was up about 4.0%.\n- `codex_local_response_latency_per_turn` was up about 8.3%.\n- The primary activity metrics also moved down: `codex_turns` about\n-6.6%, `codex_dau` about -1.0%, and `codex_local_hourly_active_users`\nabout -3.0%.\n\nAt the same time, the per-response metrics moved in the other direction:\nblended tokens per response, output tokens per response, and latency per\nresponse were all lower in test. That suggests the bad turn-level shape\nis largely about extra tool/model cycles, not each response being slower\nor more expensive on its own.\n\nLocal Windows benchmarking showed the likely mechanism: shell-wrapped\ncommands pay a large PowerShell startup/teardown tax before the actual\ncommand has much time to run. In the benchmark, the PowerShell wrapper\nadded roughly 0.7-1.0s versus direct exec:\n\n- Windows PowerShell: about 740ms p50 / 800ms p90 overhead versus direct\nexec.\n- PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`): about 930ms p50 / 980ms p90 overhead versus\ndirect exec.\n\nThe model commonly asks for a 1s initial yield. On Windows, that can\nspend nearly the whole window waiting on PowerShell machinery, so\notherwise-short commands are more likely to return as background\nsessions and require follow-up polling/tool calls.\n\nThis is intentionally a temporary unlock. It gives Windows closer to the\nsame useful post-shell command window as other platforms while we work\non reducing the PowerShell tax directly, for example with persistent\nPowerShell workers or conservative direct-exec paths for commands that\ndo not need shell semantics.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a Windows-only 2s floor to `unified_exec`'s initial\n`yield_time_ms` clamp.\n- Keeps larger model-requested waits unchanged, including the existing\n10s default.\n- Keeps the existing 30s max clamp.\n- Leaves non-Windows behavior unchanged.\n- Adds platform-gated tests for both the Windows floor and the\nnon-Windows clamp behavior.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core unified_exec`","verified_at":"2026-06-15T20:56:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7a9988d1abfedf67ecf5ae03ce15ecd0b9d82a1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e7a9988d1abfedf67ecf5ae03ce15ecd0b9d82a1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7a9988d1abfedf67ecf5ae03ce15ecd0b9d82a1/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c0b36d234a8cdbd9aa0790f5a8cbf73b7456d915","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c0b36d234a8cdbd9aa0790f5a8cbf73b7456d915","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c0b36d234a8cdbd9aa0790f5a8cbf73b7456d915"}]},{"sha":"c0b36d234a8cdbd9aa0790f5a8cbf73b7456d915","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMwYjM2ZDIzNGE4Y2RiZDlhYTA3OTBmNWE4Y2JmNzNiNzQ1NmQ5MTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T20:54:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T20:54:24Z"},"message":"recover stale Windows sandbox credentials (#27944)\n\n## Why\n\nThe elevated Windows sandbox persists dedicated sandbox account\ncredentials so later commands can launch without reprovisioning. If\nthose persisted credentials drift from the actual Windows account\npassword, `CreateProcessWithLogonW` fails with `ERROR_LOGON_FAILURE` and\nCodex currently surfaces that as a hard runner launch failure.\n\nThis change makes that failure self-healing. When Windows specifically\nrejects the sandbox login, Codex now treats the persisted sandbox\ncredentials as stale, regenerates them through the existing setup path,\nand retries the runner launch once.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Preserve `CreateProcessWithLogonW` failures as a typed runner logon\nerror so callers can distinguish `ERROR_LOGON_FAILURE` from unrelated\nlaunch failures.\n- Add a sandbox credential refresh helper that deletes the persisted\n`sandbox_users.json` record and reuses `require_logon_sandbox_creds()`\nto reprovision credentials through the established setup flow.\n- Retry elevated runner startup after stale-credential failures in both\nthe legacy elevated capture path and unified exec elevated backend.\n- Add focused tests for stale logon failure detection and persisted\nsandbox user file removal.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `cargo test -p codex-windows-sandbox`","tree":{"sha":"594aaea2dc0399de8e69ba8d226b789ccdb5f208","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/594aaea2dc0399de8e69ba8d226b789ccdb5f208"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c0b36d234a8cdbd9aa0790f5a8cbf73b7456d915","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMGaACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvJoQAEjdPQ9v2pfkopFh1FqKN9MR\nWM1/rivsF0hLz8nYIFmKbT3Vo+zD8nX8bgj71n+Z48zbB7BglR8Oox50FoLGmYn+\nClKGWMAQ/dIKgfHVwW4oODObuX3v9Jd4RKq/FuV0B/rhD3XgYHwWJ94BKJ+QYayp\nrqnYbD3PdlsvCaZLUZhsxxeDUARWD8wWV1Mbj7EoxxMLBM/GhFEil/mXxkfkxtPF\nzCkwBR1vs858Fg73et2UAx2W866leDp7d0CEWOXxeeAUwsiDoTi6JZPAT5JfulpO\nDD/vtfc0khWIjDiD+Z5rgFmBMFB7VMjszZOoZPFfqIUqrRnoEO2O0L+Rj8o5DNVR\n6KWlLFPCCHswc9n97XnE34JXKjDgMi8NhHavfPqdK05UDJJz/XVizbCMmrHn7Ln+\ncK8SK4mEFXbhEs1UFlXl0vLxMgL+I3qNc/bq9PywzJRyonWMALs5P34GkvNK48M0\ndKHJkInT/JHOfKq3wdbbAsiNO5m6lT4g66mABdifRDdAl8MUbNDD4a2ef2hqqMNF\n3sFslBLZ/kXUeydb4sGWDxUazbDOTUvkd/Vgv1H+MeWmBK0ZGpOtT4a7TUdkL2Tk\nClKTMvOhZTCiGU8NKsesr3i0y3mp/rjbG6ZrO0gWlGXdlxZYc8qdDUEvmhLJ5qwJ\n71nOchtxHuyQrY0agxcg\n=+x+q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 594aaea2dc0399de8e69ba8d226b789ccdb5f208\nparent fc1fb682a7b94b8146ee1ce6b96f278669374988\nauthor iceweasel-oai <iceweasel@openai.com> 1781556864 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781556864 -0700\n\nrecover stale Windows sandbox credentials (#27944)\n\n## Why\n\nThe elevated Windows sandbox persists dedicated sandbox account\ncredentials so later commands can launch without reprovisioning. If\nthose persisted credentials drift from the actual Windows account\npassword, `CreateProcessWithLogonW` fails with `ERROR_LOGON_FAILURE` and\nCodex currently surfaces that as a hard runner launch failure.\n\nThis change makes that failure self-healing. When Windows specifically\nrejects the sandbox login, Codex now treats the persisted sandbox\ncredentials as stale, regenerates them through the existing setup path,\nand retries the runner launch once.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Preserve `CreateProcessWithLogonW` failures as a typed runner logon\nerror so callers can distinguish `ERROR_LOGON_FAILURE` from unrelated\nlaunch failures.\n- Add a sandbox credential refresh helper that deletes the persisted\n`sandbox_users.json` record and reuses `require_logon_sandbox_creds()`\nto reprovision credentials through the established setup flow.\n- Retry elevated runner startup after stale-credential failures in both\nthe legacy elevated capture path and unified exec elevated backend.\n- Add focused tests for stale logon failure detection and persisted\nsandbox user file removal.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `cargo test -p codex-windows-sandbox`","verified_at":"2026-06-15T20:54:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c0b36d234a8cdbd9aa0790f5a8cbf73b7456d915","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c0b36d234a8cdbd9aa0790f5a8cbf73b7456d915","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c0b36d234a8cdbd9aa0790f5a8cbf73b7456d915/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fc1fb682a7b94b8146ee1ce6b96f278669374988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fc1fb682a7b94b8146ee1ce6b96f278669374988","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fc1fb682a7b94b8146ee1ce6b96f278669374988"}]},{"sha":"fc1fb682a7b94b8146ee1ce6b96f278669374988","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZjMWZiNjgyYTdiOTRiODE0NmVlMWNlNmI5NmYyNzg2NjkzNzQ5ODg","commit":{"author":{"name":"charlesgong-openai","email":"charlesgong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-15T20:25:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T20:25:42Z"},"message":"[codex] Add external agent import result accounting (#28008)\n\n## Why\n\nExternal-agent imports can complete synchronously or continue in the\nbackground for plugins/sessions. Clients need a stable import id to\ncorrelate the immediate response with the eventual completion\nnotification, and the completion payload needs enough accounting to show\nwhich artifact types succeeded or failed without hiding partial\nfailures.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- `externalAgentConfig/import` now returns an `importId`;\n`externalAgentConfig/import/completed` includes the same `importId` plus\ntype-level `itemResults`.\n- Completed `itemResults` report `successCount`, `errorCount`,\n`successes`, and `rawErrors` for each migrated item type.\n- Added protocol/schema/TypeScript types for import successes, raw\nerrors, and type-level results. No progress notification is included in\nthe final PR.\n- `ExternalAgentConfigService::import` now returns an outcome object\nwith synchronous item results and pending plugin imports.\n- Plugin import outcomes track succeeded/failed marketplaces, plugin\nids, and raw errors. Plugin failures can be reported in completed\naccounting while later migration items continue.\n- Non-plugin synchronous import failures still fail the request, so\ninvalid config/skills-style failures are not reported as a successful\nimport response.\n- Session imports now return item results. Successful imports include\nthe source session path and imported thread id; prepare, persist,\nledger, and source-validation failures become raw errors in completion\naccounting where the import can continue.\n- The request processor generates the `importId`, aggregates synchronous\nresults with background plugin/session results, and sends a single\ncompleted notification when all selected work is done.\n- App-server docs and generated schema fixtures were updated for the new\nresponse/completed payload shapes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-client event_requires_delivery`\n- `CODEX_SQLITE_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-app-server-review-sync-error\njust test -p codex-app-server\nexternal_agent_config_import_returns_error_for_failed_sync_import`\n- `CODEX_SQLITE_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-app-server-review-external-agent\njust test -p codex-app-server external_agent_config`\n\nNote: local sandbox validation used `CODEX_SQLITE_HOME` because the\ndefault sqlite state path is read-only in this environment.","tree":{"sha":"63f7c703426b7d29901bc9191a6b840e42f357b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/63f7c703426b7d29901bc9191a6b840e42f357b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fc1fb682a7b94b8146ee1ce6b96f278669374988","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMF/GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD+gQAKJWsf66ntcrPXeCsx5KSKct\nWHo3ss9z14zcvUyMd9S2khKJSJuMOwH6+VYva9iSFm5sr1d7WDzmV7qZs4eusghA\nQuTKD57uKzkgfKfn4Bpq/Oq7jh1kBTwTZpgaZGPnIEqQMwavsaWgCFDtfBP/7+IP\nzO7qaD2z24NcTNAZlfB3olIl08OoPgTpc+C4I5zXIBHfx+19er/IuraDpiaK43CU\ng3qKNDVnc0m2Yni4sOQ5j4KY6miGBsKeDSnZ72UrYi/XWaTDqgun2mf9g9IKNjhS\n2byetX2gpkNRzyQNbcVfg7wus/hnvS63BJtJZ7BDn91qu+eF4WoKNflIW7qbXo8q\n2oXzG8mIrKHSGwLGP69wA/h4RWa8oJzU+PVTjcyEw8pl9a/ik1X8Lg5h2zAUV3Tv\n2PohVaDd3Q3bH8oFXlADZIwyLLIDMHBLEjPrMe+rtYXQGVd1BByv6vjqCFyjc82g\nDF5g9z3rzOIwcG2vM+FfzmYyCsmbS+rPobnBDp3vznLFteSCvlt+YHquO/+rpGcx\nCZEdtOmHmzG04vj1BcS+kBPgl1hv8KXqaFeWw9Txng7XR43nhRi5QLy9suJkj0e3\nvj2yaQRxABPs3fE5Ip2qck8Szm+oI5TTuhLqu5KIXJlHS1BfXI2R/cBvMyVW/XYP\nI28SYOtCwG0ohCprfYOh\n=wV/J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 63f7c703426b7d29901bc9191a6b840e42f357b7\nparent 41db093aa0a32010b49ee51dbe5aa33e49467fd7\nauthor charlesgong-openai <charlesgong@openai.com> 1781555142 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781555142 -0700\n\n[codex] Add external agent import result accounting (#28008)\n\n## Why\n\nExternal-agent imports can complete synchronously or continue in the\nbackground for plugins/sessions. Clients need a stable import id to\ncorrelate the immediate response with the eventual completion\nnotification, and the completion payload needs enough accounting to show\nwhich artifact types succeeded or failed without hiding partial\nfailures.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- `externalAgentConfig/import` now returns an `importId`;\n`externalAgentConfig/import/completed` includes the same `importId` plus\ntype-level `itemResults`.\n- Completed `itemResults` report `successCount`, `errorCount`,\n`successes`, and `rawErrors` for each migrated item type.\n- Added protocol/schema/TypeScript types for import successes, raw\nerrors, and type-level results. No progress notification is included in\nthe final PR.\n- `ExternalAgentConfigService::import` now returns an outcome object\nwith synchronous item results and pending plugin imports.\n- Plugin import outcomes track succeeded/failed marketplaces, plugin\nids, and raw errors. Plugin failures can be reported in completed\naccounting while later migration items continue.\n- Non-plugin synchronous import failures still fail the request, so\ninvalid config/skills-style failures are not reported as a successful\nimport response.\n- Session imports now return item results. Successful imports include\nthe source session path and imported thread id; prepare, persist,\nledger, and source-validation failures become raw errors in completion\naccounting where the import can continue.\n- The request processor generates the `importId`, aggregates synchronous\nresults with background plugin/session results, and sends a single\ncompleted notification when all selected work is done.\n- App-server docs and generated schema fixtures were updated for the new\nresponse/completed payload shapes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-client event_requires_delivery`\n- `CODEX_SQLITE_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-app-server-review-sync-error\njust test -p codex-app-server\nexternal_agent_config_import_returns_error_for_failed_sync_import`\n- `CODEX_SQLITE_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-app-server-review-external-agent\njust test -p codex-app-server external_agent_config`\n\nNote: local sandbox validation used `CODEX_SQLITE_HOME` because the\ndefault sqlite state path is read-only in this environment.","verified_at":"2026-06-15T20:25:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fc1fb682a7b94b8146ee1ce6b96f278669374988","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fc1fb682a7b94b8146ee1ce6b96f278669374988","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fc1fb682a7b94b8146ee1ce6b96f278669374988/comments","author":{"login":"charlesgong-openai","id":200841148,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_iXvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200841148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesgong-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"htt