ext_turn`\n- `just test -p codex-cli mcp`\n- `just fix -p codex-rmcp-client -p codex-mcp -p codex-core -p codex-cli\n-p codex-app-server -p codex-protocol`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","verified_at":"2026-06-12T22:03:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9915d34684c5cf6cca5c9674d5684300c5995af6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9915d34684c5cf6cca5c9674d5684300c5995af6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9915d34684c5cf6cca5c9674d5684300c5995af6/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4d1702586a4acdc88e2c261f4e4630e016e5fbe7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4d1702586a4acdc88e2c261f4e4630e016e5fbe7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4d1702586a4acdc88e2c261f4e4630e016e5fbe7"}]},{"sha":"4d1702586a4acdc88e2c261f4e4630e016e5fbe7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRkMTcwMjU4NmE0YWNkYzg4ZTJjMjYxZjRlNDYzMGUwMTZlNWZiZTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"canvrno-oai","email":"kbond@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T21:52:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T21:52:07Z"},"message":"Warn for structured feature toggles (#27076)\n\n## Summary\nStartup warnings for under-development features only recognized bare\nboolean toggles like `features.foo = true`. An upcoming feature will use\ntable-format config, so `features.foo = { enabled = true, ... }` needs\nto count as an explicit opt-in too.\n\nThis updates the warning predicate to recognize structured tables with\n`enabled = true`, while leaving tables without that field unwarned.\n\n## Testing\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-features\nunstable_warning_event_mentions_enabled_structured_under_development_feature`","tree":{"sha":"2f735b7a7a223a52f578d90ab523d696bc318882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2f735b7a7a223a52f578d90ab523d696bc318882"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4d1702586a4acdc88e2c261f4e4630e016e5fbe7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLH+HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArpkQADZd29So4hB9+rQhyquyvcmC\nvzDgLsbfQM6QpGSU8r1qduQ1OyW786m67jevu/g3CiGUDH8WWnatkQuAdq4wQksP\nOiZfjmN9tY88rw/Zl/cf3TVBNNpZfu/5eHR8U0gy+tsqOJTddbP/VdVdR0Rxr/0E\niVUjmBE5PSVOGUKmAgiJfG6nEpfVvqNvLmFmdieUQkpr4poUARn08/tz8Z1pTqfq\niJ2/lFXtmWHxj3dDDbv386T8oAXXEl4mGtIwH1uFk69V4bbvGe7tjzOcilQdtZ3M\n5hDDVdF23xSAb/7KxTuStsnueV+wMtOKjEmHGsCt8Nxgc+uGhD0TaNKjRkPI0fYC\nheYV9yGVa/DcL93Vj6oi4gMzB5o+9SNulr0/xDLeQ19GIurQVDgCBNrZLODe3iJV\nUpzYSFaGqTzLlxfSWQUyALPYJ8biNs0X7cBcLOWnf0GUWHv/XZ05ErHPg1J19zv9\nPoPvB6cIW+HAe+t+82PPuZO15qBnBPdmdkRxEliGRHIjkwT0kXsBck53pjc4FJjy\nmmHKZ0UAmMRQfkhnPliUaxrjs4tM/vamx4M1qH28lxlskCN1QOpz+E9Le54uCWuJ\nm1lNY7N385TSbw/PGFs03htpzAloMZrMlOkD3l+lZfn73/kyuCtPuMcxuNyJRT8V\nRsAMM3+o1dPIixL7mhHU\n=QVAz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2f735b7a7a223a52f578d90ab523d696bc318882\nparent 56c97e3b5c8430613afc6d782ab7463bce8df812\nauthor canvrno-oai <kbond@openai.com> 1781301127 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781301127 -0700\n\nWarn for structured feature toggles (#27076)\n\n## Summary\nStartup warnings for under-development features only recognized bare\nboolean toggles like `features.foo = true`. An upcoming feature will use\ntable-format config, so `features.foo = { enabled = true, ... }` needs\nto count as an explicit opt-in too.\n\nThis updates the warning predicate to recognize structured tables with\n`enabled = true`, while leaving tables without that field unwarned.\n\n## Testing\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-features\nunstable_warning_event_mentions_enabled_structured_under_development_feature`","verified_at":"2026-06-12T21:52:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4d1702586a4acdc88e2c261f4e4630e016e5fbe7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4d1702586a4acdc88e2c261f4e4630e016e5fbe7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4d1702586a4acdc88e2c261f4e4630e016e5fbe7/comments","author":{"login":"canvrno-oai","id":257630656,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1shwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257630656?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/canvrno-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"56c97e3b5c8430613afc6d782ab7463bce8df812","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/56c97e3b5c8430613afc6d782ab7463bce8df812","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/56c97e3b5c8430613afc6d782ab7463bce8df812"}]},{"sha":"56c97e3b5c8430613afc6d782ab7463bce8df812","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU2Yzk3ZTNiNWM4NDMwNjEzYWZjNmQ3ODJhYjc0NjNiY2U4ZGY4MTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T21:23:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T21:23:50Z"},"message":"feat: use encrypted local secrets for CLI auth (#27539)\n\n## Why\n\nWindows Credential Manager limits generic credential blobs to 2,560\nbytes. Large serialized ChatGPT auth payloads can exceed that limit, so\nkeyring-mode CLI auth needs a backend that keeps only the encryption key\nin the OS keyring and stores the payload in Codex's encrypted\nlocal-secrets file.\n\nThis is the third PR in the encrypted-auth stack:\n\n1. #27504 — feature and config selection\n2. #27535 — auth-specific local-secrets namespaces\n3. This PR — CLI auth implementation and activation\n4. MCP OAuth implementation and activation\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added encrypted CLI-auth storage using the `CliAuth` secrets\nnamespace.\n- Preserved direct keyring storage for platforms/configurations where it\nremains selected.\n- Selected the backend consistently for login, logout, refresh,\ndevice-code login, auth loading, and login restrictions.\n- Threaded resolved bootstrap/full config through CLI, exec, TUI,\napp-server account handling, cloud config, and cloud tasks.\n- Removed stale `auth.json` fallback data after successful encrypted\nsaves and removed encrypted, direct-keyring, and fallback data during\nlogout.\n- Added storage and integration coverage for both direct and encrypted\nkeyring modes.\n\nMCP OAuth persistence is intentionally left to the next PR.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-login` — 131 passed\n- `just test -p codex-cli` — 280 passed\n- `just test -p codex-app-server v2::account` — 25 passed\n- `just test -p codex-cloud-config service` — 21 passed, 7 skipped\n- `just fix -p codex-login`\n- `just fix -p codex-cli`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"c7e3f63e92cb05a82a558d044fd14653e3efc7fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c7e3f63e92cb05a82a558d044fd14653e3efc7fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/56c97e3b5c8430613afc6d782ab7463bce8df812","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLHjmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY4EQAAo+i+inIRgmtJnpLYYlOCso\nqXP5Kl9HqN+Orb9dke2iBLEBqv+P6uyc1YwTYEg+oGSCUQ6qZaiVekkE96Hr2BYh\nHxNryP6C1diCdayaH/bmOjShvEOXHU+LEoh2xF1GDPxc6GuwlcuP9O6haoo5z89U\nJIYfhmsDJ4CVMjtKFiw1O0rqNjfUVmjZwyyPBD0lk7YZnttcVGjwVMjRp2E8kZpU\n0hdeT/fG/RKKgjjGUgSI2vWpReYrYHOo2M1z+QWvgzIXm30b94xvjcoY2niYc1gC\nRQgpSuTtvVCMqYEeEKwmjOkLEoGrMaQoTDcYGk37UrWafX0zps/y8Jp9zz5PeBGs\nYgJQzUPULw7wW8S9c/668QGGtTliFA+tas5qWOAxeTTujZL+E7gSddlGu0etU8cV\nGGEvS0+ZoqZpUikyrOlJZ4GwrOUAX67Ly4uKgrk0UeCpvf09/jbpF0y5/N3jSyFh\nh/dSD5IPIIfbnNr/nIrZvQ9w0wZJkTs+n4cN0HmsCx7Cdg9nS7unm33Z86S7gNJ+\nW/VP1EP7BtU9pt3ej1iI0/xbMgu8l79/OXcSNVhhdz0nxjfQEjrnmOmU2yQ0Vn9a\nM79U53Hrm1K629cGmf/ljIxTZX+RlpTuvSPUo01swqDDgJ65O3hL4EmRfnGdKwno\nE4DP7OuKGmA/b+nex+Bt\n=cIjc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c7e3f63e92cb05a82a558d044fd14653e3efc7fe\nparent 576f6034406795cc6d9b35113e5fa96dc34997f1\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1781299430 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781299430 +0000\n\nfeat: use encrypted local secrets for CLI auth (#27539)\n\n## Why\n\nWindows Credential Manager limits generic credential blobs to 2,560\nbytes. Large serialized ChatGPT auth payloads can exceed that limit, so\nkeyring-mode CLI auth needs a backend that keeps only the encryption key\nin the OS keyring and stores the payload in Codex's encrypted\nlocal-secrets file.\n\nThis is the third PR in the encrypted-auth stack:\n\n1. #27504 — feature and config selection\n2. #27535 — auth-specific local-secrets namespaces\n3. This PR — CLI auth implementation and activation\n4. MCP OAuth implementation and activation\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added encrypted CLI-auth storage using the `CliAuth` secrets\nnamespace.\n- Preserved direct keyring storage for platforms/configurations where it\nremains selected.\n- Selected the backend consistently for login, logout, refresh,\ndevice-code login, auth loading, and login restrictions.\n- Threaded resolved bootstrap/full config through CLI, exec, TUI,\napp-server account handling, cloud config, and cloud tasks.\n- Removed stale `auth.json` fallback data after successful encrypted\nsaves and removed encrypted, direct-keyring, and fallback data during\nlogout.\n- Added storage and integration coverage for both direct and encrypted\nkeyring modes.\n\nMCP OAuth persistence is intentionally left to the next PR.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-login` — 131 passed\n- `just test -p codex-cli` — 280 passed\n- `just test -p codex-app-server v2::account` — 25 passed\n- `just test -p codex-cloud-config service` — 21 passed, 7 skipped\n- `just fix -p codex-login`\n- `just fix -p codex-cli`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-12T21:23:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/56c97e3b5c8430613afc6d782ab7463bce8df812","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/56c97e3b5c8430613afc6d782ab7463bce8df812","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/56c97e3b5c8430613afc6d782ab7463bce8df812/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"576f6034406795cc6d9b35113e5fa96dc34997f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/576f6034406795cc6d9b35113e5fa96dc34997f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/576f6034406795cc6d9b35113e5fa96dc34997f1"}]},{"sha":"576f6034406795cc6d9b35113e5fa96dc34997f1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU3NmY2MDM0NDA2Nzk1Y2M2ZDliMzUxMTNlNWZhOTZkYzM0OTk3ZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T21:20:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T21:20:55Z"},"message":"Remove TUI realtime voice support (#27801)\n\n## Why\n\nRemoves the realtime audio support from TUI.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Removed the TUI `/realtime` and realtime `/settings` command paths.\n- Deleted TUI voice capture/playback, WebRTC session handling,\naudio-device selection UI, and recording-meter code.\n- Removed TUI realtime tests and snapshots that covered the deleted\nsurfaces.\n- Dropped the TUI-only `cpal` and `codex-realtime-webrtc` dependencies\nand refreshed the Rust/Bazel locks.","tree":{"sha":"f9595d38af17e0c7bbb26f2f7980ae98ec414c98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f9595d38af17e0c7bbb26f2f7980ae98ec414c98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/576f6034406795cc6d9b35113e5fa96dc34997f1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLHg3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOXYQADKjGZFiFXksWpt+VEWUH1uB\ni022SqzWuHj/v3oLwH8Qf6ZzCGRR3gCn5ltbrTBzhrmHnYMtD/6Zy4C4ExpC6rrf\nsmZFBDooy/BN15FcgJAKnsHtCrX2vj7WGlvzvPiwV3keMK6p+n5P+1oWnvHrLgZ8\nr3h+Jd8t4cqY9hyYJwZ3+QPrBRwRbBgX6F9Ad1R/IxtIBrSs1GCdrWtznI/Jxp4G\nWeIMnuaDWHwoU58lcIlx5Gni1+WtQofVjp9tPPZ+Hpx5Ue/MR9bDKZbFRLqm2T5w\nb5v9hvRr1Oax8C6uV3+PmGsz4Up9a79+4sHL5flZhejkwxoAOiBEyEZW96TAIZfv\n7uGhWftSQw1WeKEYJBpgNhsRAd3Dyv/EolbyaNhMDyfvu7J26jkefcvmgrhw1EI9\nH1l8zZq95E0YS3/7qO5xOo9hTR078uVqTSBPDjkPX7TwVVrjkmMcW2gvNqSDcDrN\noQxjI8JvYPCglkSyDPPcqhxQNLHkkAz8mUovejJlaVmGGF/SYdvrNj5ULu8VjLbL\nOnadIbWnrOiKVl+QKogzp4C6Eng+qVqubsHGBzHiPjBjsQsYAFxIfjJdc6owMwip\nfk/24Z2WBi1zvthC+n8dgsOv6xrTM+obnKw3p6kmKa3cj+o6JBoVxbiIgtaEm1bT\nZznKAAmkrnkDE8TkRTB+\n=jwuq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f9595d38af17e0c7bbb26f2f7980ae98ec414c98\nparent 8f2d6416ce41be54551185c640f83e22f061eccd\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1781299255 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781299255 -0700\n\nRemove TUI realtime voice support (#27801)\n\n## Why\n\nRemoves the realtime audio support from TUI.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Removed the TUI `/realtime` and realtime `/settings` command paths.\n- Deleted TUI voice capture/playback, WebRTC session handling,\naudio-device selection UI, and recording-meter code.\n- Removed TUI realtime tests and snapshots that covered the deleted\nsurfaces.\n- Dropped the TUI-only `cpal` and `codex-realtime-webrtc` dependencies\nand refreshed the Rust/Bazel locks.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T21:20:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/576f6034406795cc6d9b35113e5fa96dc34997f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/576f6034406795cc6d9b35113e5fa96dc34997f1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/576f6034406795cc6d9b35113e5fa96dc34997f1/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8f2d6416ce41be54551185c640f83e22f061eccd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f2d6416ce41be54551185c640f83e22f061eccd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8f2d6416ce41be54551185c640f83e22f061eccd"}]},{"sha":"8f2d6416ce41be54551185c640f83e22f061eccd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhmMmQ2NDE2Y2U0MWJlNTQ1NTExODVjNjQwZjgzZTIyZjA2MWVjY2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T20:50:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T20:50:04Z"},"message":"Support plaintext agent messages (#27830)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 `send_message` deliveries already reach the receiving\nmodel as typed `agent_message` items with encrypted content.\nChild-completion notifications are generated by Codex itself, so their\ncontent is plaintext and previously fell back to a serialized JSON\nenvelope inside an assistant message.\n\nWith plaintext `input_text` supported for `agent_message`, both delivery\npaths can use the same model-visible type while preserving explicit\nauthor and recipient metadata.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add plaintext `input_text` support to `AgentMessageInputContent` and\nregenerate the affected app-server schemas\n- preserve `InterAgentCommunication` as structured mailbox input instead\nof converting it to assistant text\n- record delivered communications as typed `agent_message` history items\n- persist a dedicated rollout item so local delivery metadata such as\n`trigger_turn` remains available without leaking into the Responses\nrequest\n- reconstruct typed agent messages on resume and preserve fork-turn\ntruncation behavior\n- remove request-time assistant-content parsing\n- preserve plaintext and encrypted inter-agent deliveries in stage-one\nmemory inputs\n- normalize and link plaintext and encrypted agent messages in rollout\ntraces without treating inbound messages as child results\n- cover the real MultiAgent V2 child-completion path end to end with\ndeterministic mailbox synchronization\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nplaintext_multi_agent_v2_completion_sends_agent_message`\n- `just test -p codex-core input_queue_drains_mailbox_in_delivery_order\nrecord_initial_history_reconstructs_typed_inter_agent_message\nfork_turn_positions_use_inter_agent_delivery_metadata`\n- `just test -p codex-memories-write\nserializes_inter_agent_communications_for_memory`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout-trace\nagent_messages_preserve_routing_and_content\nsub_agent_started_activity_creates_spawn_edge`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout-trace\nagent_result_edge_falls_back_to_child_thread_without_result_message`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol -p codex-rollout -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol`","tree":{"sha":"4e16f90680c70fd590953b9ef96d1593f8d7015e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4e16f90680c70fd590953b9ef96d1593f8d7015e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8f2d6416ce41be54551185c640f83e22f061eccd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLHD8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2cEQAK+hQWXxWe7In9tEJ2OzFw1r\n4ECkRB/o5ksLxHY3epsohTwYInmNYjhVbajuQt4cAFdUEfW48YcuOXMW5F4MBWmX\nbwV2XfCuGTw8bv1epoh8EG5s618S5HKYPTcdZVIkCA5wWYTyahEU2uAXUjuhugG9\nMMVDqqsf3J0hihGSCT1ceVpcKO/ORS1Oh+51Ptrvo08TF6QdB1E+AHyECXOgH+YD\n+xiR9f/XftSoAy3RmyzYQy6XiV7H9DUvUDAG7ivMBLXSBzH3KqeEPsXdyk9nHvRA\ntmM1c0wXWC5B+dpx7WbOP2mZ9UCGCfML442qBmsPMD+c03ZWtio/7VZozcOkdY7n\nJXpaGXqEDpD/hFCkvD3ffT688hDSmEZHU89WkKxkjqvXaMoiEQTGgUvy5MLfar8/\ndJyd/1wzO+AbyVZrvBHOR+Oha1DW9acNOl+gcUN2C9ahX8h/WbsyGWJjbJH5uwDw\njdB2sHwIWZpEu7pXCQFMMoPOXHpi5YFb7IKBMkAwX2/sam/bmSdgttGb6la9pCT6\nqEtS561B62XA43NUCUH1baok1vT7mNkS5G4WWt6vJEB7mDuDUUmVp6VWX1B5R9qT\nuDRyb1ampDAZOrOPKIupZpL5f7TaPegN1AWQ4zI+KhbVjySBbcjh19/Wjzc+Tdef\nQnRw4tcwNvGop1umHdXD\n=pxho\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4e16f90680c70fd590953b9ef96d1593f8d7015e\nparent 3e2ee1da3fe3cb078cad46c450a8cabae30edffe\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781297404 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781297404 -0700\n\nSupport plaintext agent messages (#27830)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 `send_message` deliveries already reach the receiving\nmodel as typed `agent_message` items with encrypted content.\nChild-completion notifications are generated by Codex itself, so their\ncontent is plaintext and previously fell back to a serialized JSON\nenvelope inside an assistant message.\n\nWith plaintext `input_text` supported for `agent_message`, both delivery\npaths can use the same model-visible type while preserving explicit\nauthor and recipient metadata.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add plaintext `input_text` support to `AgentMessageInputContent` and\nregenerate the affected app-server schemas\n- preserve `InterAgentCommunication` as structured mailbox input instead\nof converting it to assistant text\n- record delivered communications as typed `agent_message` history items\n- persist a dedicated rollout item so local delivery metadata such as\n`trigger_turn` remains available without leaking into the Responses\nrequest\n- reconstruct typed agent messages on resume and preserve fork-turn\ntruncation behavior\n- remove request-time assistant-content parsing\n- preserve plaintext and encrypted inter-agent deliveries in stage-one\nmemory inputs\n- normalize and link plaintext and encrypted agent messages in rollout\ntraces without treating inbound messages as child results\n- cover the real MultiAgent V2 child-completion path end to end with\ndeterministic mailbox synchronization\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nplaintext_multi_agent_v2_completion_sends_agent_message`\n- `just test -p codex-core input_queue_drains_mailbox_in_delivery_order\nrecord_initial_history_reconstructs_typed_inter_agent_message\nfork_turn_positions_use_inter_agent_delivery_metadata`\n- `just test -p codex-memories-write\nserializes_inter_agent_communications_for_memory`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout-trace\nagent_messages_preserve_routing_and_content\nsub_agent_started_activity_creates_spawn_edge`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout-trace\nagent_result_edge_falls_back_to_child_thread_without_result_message`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol -p codex-rollout -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol`","verified_at":"2026-06-12T20:50:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f2d6416ce41be54551185c640f83e22f061eccd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8f2d6416ce41be54551185c640f83e22f061eccd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f2d6416ce41be54551185c640f83e22f061eccd/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.co