d-oai","id":220976066,"node_id":"U_kgDODSvTwg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220976066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/dylan-hurd-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a57087a8654ddca712461720f3a3ed258e29033b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a57087a8654ddca712461720f3a3ed258e29033b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a57087a8654ddca712461720f3a3ed258e29033b"}]},{"sha":"a57087a8654ddca712461720f3a3ed258e29033b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE1NzA4N2E4NjU0ZGRjYTcxMjQ2MTcyMGYzYTNlZDI1OGUyOTAzM2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"alexsong-oai","email":"alexsong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T20:23:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T20:23:22Z"},"message":"[codex] Align implicit skill reads with parser (#27926)\n\n## Summary\n- reuse the shared shell read parser for implicit skill doc invocation\ndetection\n- add regression coverage for `nl -ba .../SKILL.md`\n\n## Why\nDesktop could render `Read User Context skill` for reads recognized by\nthe shared command parser, while implicit `skill_invocation` analytics\nused a separate reader allowlist and missed cases such as `nl`.\n\n## Validation\n- `HOME=/private/tmp/codex-core-skills-home-pr\nPATH=/Users/alexsong/.cache/cargo-home/bin:$PATH\nCARGO_HOME=/Users/alexsong/.cache/cargo-home just test -p\ncodex-core-skills`\n- `git diff --cached --check`\n- `just fmt` attempted; Rust formatting completed, but the Python\nformatters could not download uncached Ruff wheels because\n`files.pythonhosted.org` is blocked in this sandbox.\n- `bazel mod deps --lockfile_mode=update/error\n--repo_env=ASPECT_TOOLS_TELEMETRY= --repo_env=DO_NOT_TRACK=1` evaluated\nthe module graph and produced no `MODULE.bazel.lock` diff, but Bazel\ncrashed on sandboxed `sysctl` during exit.","tree":{"sha":"2cc9d840a95bad1fa7834a33d8b8769d23a19554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2cc9d840a95bad1fa7834a33d8b8769d23a19554"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a57087a8654ddca712461720f3a3ed258e29033b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLGq6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8x8QAEkOkfqWkL0jxDkW4V55BIaV\nxtmXIN2gBpHVW4nHyS1F+Fr9JPQLbJqO6F3LWM6ACs4HmTOqOfPzBdiNL2LihyVW\ns36mnBxXy/cYfm2v1y5+7uHibh44RGPZXHtIxSOAHoFgbVDxuxOdy3h0JUTRS8pn\n/QmqhsbFdDubqaR9Z+DHEntuGOHxTIoQ2jzztTv6ENCRPxHjDQ/XVBJufomceim2\nMhBQLxAqdUuFA6ujlyxRF4cHcNXeBeKhAICfEL0nnKz2rzl3UtgBGGpZKUZaIJRG\nRShqyKjXdPubJgkOv7epKDh/d4kN9cvFiJt7aYetJNl6djNnA9I8p1ipZC5mJ9nP\n6fEZMactDfjYiAyMoeg7fzcVW6BVQDcf4EwWSACVaY3cxtE6KOGZl64+3byX5p+a\ndCmRAqQh3XYvPA8WvzEL2zubkPFHDgb9T3wBRqE9li2ogMOOnG1BW6c/gVjBNuIw\n/wQsPugmu0knoJB2hxQkf2q6q7S63Ob7NJGKAQ66nc3OfWfuXcQUHm2HYFK2xrFT\nwkV4h8A/23d40dA7y/iNW1XnIQnQYBkuonVEbNPA+5gMWDHOUKEBQn09FUpPMUWK\nXGP77pHgBNXZBwG/Q1xlx7FiU06qVt7A6b9rp/cS3MWIZ3JDcr3PNZDpnplV1Xkw\nf8Z82tCeh5X0GzmnsF6f\n=gp5Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2cc9d840a95bad1fa7834a33d8b8769d23a19554\nparent 2ee854eaa5efc9f5d3952825f13cb0905fcde2c9\nauthor alexsong-oai <alexsong@openai.com> 1781295802 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781295802 -0700\n\n[codex] Align implicit skill reads with parser (#27926)\n\n## Summary\n- reuse the shared shell read parser for implicit skill doc invocation\ndetection\n- add regression coverage for `nl -ba .../SKILL.md`\n\n## Why\nDesktop could render `Read User Context skill` for reads recognized by\nthe shared command parser, while implicit `skill_invocation` analytics\nused a separate reader allowlist and missed cases such as `nl`.\n\n## Validation\n- `HOME=/private/tmp/codex-core-skills-home-pr\nPATH=/Users/alexsong/.cache/cargo-home/bin:$PATH\nCARGO_HOME=/Users/alexsong/.cache/cargo-home just test -p\ncodex-core-skills`\n- `git diff --cached --check`\n- `just fmt` attempted; Rust formatting completed, but the Python\nformatters could not download uncached Ruff wheels because\n`files.pythonhosted.org` is blocked in this sandbox.\n- `bazel mod deps --lockfile_mode=update/error\n--repo_env=ASPECT_TOOLS_TELEMETRY= --repo_env=DO_NOT_TRACK=1` evaluated\nthe module graph and produced no `MODULE.bazel.lock` diff, but Bazel\ncrashed on sandboxed `sysctl` during exit.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T20:23:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a57087a8654ddca712461720f3a3ed258e29033b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a57087a8654ddca712461720f3a3ed258e29033b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a57087a8654ddca712461720f3a3ed258e29033b/comments","author":{"login":"alexsong-oai","id":256201575,"node_id":"U_kgDOD0VTZw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256201575?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/alexsong-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2ee854eaa5efc9f5d3952825f13cb0905fcde2c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2ee854eaa5efc9f5d3952825f13cb0905fcde2c9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2ee854eaa5efc9f5d3952825f13cb0905fcde2c9"}]},{"sha":"2ee854eaa5efc9f5d3952825f13cb0905fcde2c9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJlZTg1NGVhYTVlZmM5ZjVkMzk1MjgyNWYxM2NiMDkwNWZjZGUyYzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T20:00:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T20:00:21Z"},"message":"[codex] Add crate API surface review rule (#27939)\n\n## Why\n\nReview guidance should explicitly discourage widening crate APIs for\ntesting convenience. Keeping those boundaries narrow reduces accidental\ncoupling and prevents one-off test utilities from becoming durable\npublic surface area.\n\n## What\n\n- Add a crate API surface rule to `AGENTS.md`.\n- Ask reviewers to keep crate APIs small and avoid proliferating\ntest-only helpers.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Not run (documentation-only change).","tree":{"sha":"0195cf2a28de256e84df39f2c454a8d76bd48f8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0195cf2a28de256e84df39f2c454a8d76bd48f8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2ee854eaa5efc9f5d3952825f13cb0905fcde2c9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLGVVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC9IQAK01wdTPfDqpV7Mc/m26ipRF\nUtsSdEZdaG99ZuaYPu5FpCoO1r1Nx68yWD0AftjaE1SLvAPCHnPW2OqyGrZJcZR4\nO4J0sgB3+Af/BVTShzZ4gJxiOj1GOQH+usIBa6ZlXv1hZyqm2CYi+/c6tD2aloN8\nlPDlIILmdw2779OFaFJkitOvw21zIMZfCGhBtB+ASYMjpCXLKGO+/wLbqSDznupH\nSM/CCVLrdGxFvbx+QwRQafuUz3FqrFxZZE5FSUjYorTSTgnlqznmYlevhmBkj1Xu\nVuGc2qsjzhgM+Ywgev1sw+gv3zH2rdHw4riEyVhLtaho9ZJdc4xxamCnxN5Y64q7\nxlL56uI0MUG66+CQ9D6wCV2Pyi/mFGs6vRluGVxNjQdUxsnpLoi154jgxMZ5c46c\nfVo/XItvvEOnGIkHxhHboBW+WsBuyg/V2bOtgv91GHFjLVQzpggwAe8y4yrAy8/C\nw0y3LSOcp7jOlrFWWwsPjCtR0IYwXKpbKzcKJ1LZmAi85U60akq4sqim/BPCAOS1\nayeNKFiNKZvLP7mbkpwvh5rzcqXNW0SwwlvIV6jaDt5sJSAEZQ1q/i26NZ5L3lTx\nVSq8oZ2NLX9dEiLkTZp+vPr37z4HC6UhnMcHOCNpevf8U/j1MzXLhMLfe3V7IbrE\nrEarBAo+5RVKUA8Dp5bR\n=Xc3Z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0195cf2a28de256e84df39f2c454a8d76bd48f8d\nparent 7cc80b39f1247beb9319228d9b3129c510763914\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781294421 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781294421 -0700\n\n[codex] Add crate API surface review rule (#27939)\n\n## Why\n\nReview guidance should explicitly discourage widening crate APIs for\ntesting convenience. Keeping those boundaries narrow reduces accidental\ncoupling and prevents one-off test utilities from becoming durable\npublic surface area.\n\n## What\n\n- Add a crate API surface rule to `AGENTS.md`.\n- Ask reviewers to keep crate APIs small and avoid proliferating\ntest-only helpers.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Not run (documentation-only change).","verified_at":"2026-06-12T20:00:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2ee854eaa5efc9f5d3952825f13cb0905fcde2c9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2ee854eaa5efc9f5d3952825f13cb0905fcde2c9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2ee854eaa5efc9f5d3952825f13cb0905fcde2c9/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7cc80b39f1247beb9319228d9b3129c510763914","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7cc80b39f1247beb9319228d9b3129c510763914","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7cc80b39f1247beb9319228d9b3129c510763914"}]},{"sha":"7cc80b39f1247beb9319228d9b3129c510763914","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdjYzgwYjM5ZjEyNDdiZWI5MzE5MjI4ZDliMzEyOWM1MTA3NjM5MTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T19:52:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T19:52:49Z"},"message":"feat: add auth-specific encrypted secret namespaces (#27535)\n\n## Why\n\nCLI auth and MCP OAuth credentials should use separate encrypted files\nwhile sharing the existing local-secrets implementation and\nOS-keyring-backed encryption key mechanism.\n\nThis is the second PR in the encrypted-auth stack:\n\n1. #27504 — feature and config selection\n2. This PR — auth-specific local-secrets namespaces\n3. CLI auth implementation and activation\n4. MCP OAuth implementation and activation\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added `LocalSecretsNamespace` variants for shared secrets, CLI auth,\nand MCP OAuth.\n- Selected `local.age`, `cli_auth.age`, or `mcp_oauth.age` from the\nnamespace.\n- Made atomic temporary filenames derive from the selected secrets\nfilename.\n- Added namespaced `SecretsManager` construction and coverage proving\nthe auth namespaces write separate encrypted files.\n- Made the default keyring store clonable for downstream namespaced auth\nbackends.\n\nThis PR does not activate either auth backend or change existing\ncredential behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-secrets` — 7 passed\n- `just test -p codex-keyring-store` — package has no test binaries\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"704510911c87a8615aa2b523aa28ea087230871c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/704510911c87a8615aa2b523aa28ea087230871c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7cc80b39f1247beb9319228d9b3129c510763914","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLGORCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK5oQAIwi5QPeFtyQ4lXpNF0iy//e\nT02+k73eDgiVkU4eMzohlNGlx8s8/w8wrjxX8P9Rw/qopbgdVTgXgJkGBsDGqTwC\no4/S7AtKFvjilkNz81MDm/HX7AlA+Ou95Ri9X657tkES0usSrzbxgVmbRmXybiit\nzPL0zQNFJNYcXaXdLD2aKXj+E70F8LYWV0FoJR0tz4ohVFn6m1CCfSVHpHerTBIb\nnxcAolVUIDUxDMt9dwgLqYpSpxLYMmuu3Hiq3/6EK47vN2bGr9XNLr0wEnxUuxOS\nFn14EXj1dHgLG2QMdnTbUfgwrVJnfdGYhbEbbIDJHfQw5B2+lyMfP4u3LDfGo39K\nK7GDgcR1OYs6DveB41afZmc1o7AMp6K6gZjzLWhgYWd3pbRybKzfXiJkyFzfW0xX\nEIXFM7ZxIDpI7BiFxKlCvf9NIOUl4G4KBkKloLwhZH0tbTMj2/faQ/GpRWXu0bXd\nN7KnKos8tWw1ofmQVbPB5B44jz6bKkZYymNzqitViXT2/K2r+BPioxH5S3sl5khX\nyaStPDxsXoT+VxIHrp0IUe+X7z+/gnwCli6RXSATDhcbwmKIyNl+ccnkymOGGu9f\nw7XFIbBi+oZhEreBkoasibpUn4kMJUHhA93t/DEVd7sP6JVl2QSh9ZZmRWqMj9jL\nF/X+I0UXcmXXwN9MydVg\n=Sm3O\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 704510911c87a8615aa2b523aa28ea087230871c\nparent d1aaf789ade6b0f20d746e7fa7ac8a7520798456\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1781293969 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781293969 +0000\n\nfeat: add auth-specific encrypted secret namespaces (#27535)\n\n## Why\n\nCLI auth and MCP OAuth credentials should use separate encrypted files\nwhile sharing the existing local-secrets implementation and\nOS-keyring-backed encryption key mechanism.\n\nThis is the second PR in the encrypted-auth stack:\n\n1. #27504 — feature and config selection\n2. This PR — auth-specific local-secrets namespaces\n3. CLI auth implementation and activation\n4. MCP OAuth implementation and activation\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added `LocalSecretsNamespace` variants for shared secrets, CLI auth,\nand MCP OAuth.\n- Selected `local.age`, `cli_auth.age`, or `mcp_oauth.age` from the\nnamespace.\n- Made atomic temporary filenames derive from the selected secrets\nfilename.\n- Added namespaced `SecretsManager` construction and coverage proving\nthe auth namespaces write separate encrypted files.\n- Made the default keyring store clonable for downstream namespaced auth\nbackends.\n\nThis PR does not activate either auth backend or change existing\ncredential behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-secrets` — 7 passed\n- `just test -p codex-keyring-store` — package has no test binaries\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-12T19:52:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7cc80b39f1247beb9319228d9b3129c510763914","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7cc80b39f1247beb9319228d9b3129c510763914","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7cc80b39f1247beb9319228d9b3129c510763914/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d1aaf789ade6b0f20d746e7fa7ac8a7520798456","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d1aaf789ade6b0f20d746e7fa7ac8a7520798456","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d1aaf789ade6b0f20d746e7fa7ac8a7520798456"}]},{"sha":"d1aaf789ade6b0f20d746e7fa7ac8a7520798456","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQxYWFmNzg5YWRlNmIwZjIwZDc0NmU3ZmE3YWM4YTc1MjA3OTg0NTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"cooper-oai","email":"cooper@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T19:38:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T19:38:30Z"},"message":"[login] revoke existing auth before starting login (#27674)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex login` previously persisted newly issued OAuth credentials and\nonly then attempted to revoke the superseded refresh token. The old\ncredential must be revoked before a replacement browser or device-code\nflow starts, and successful login must not perform any post-login\nrevocation attempt.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Revoke and clear existing stored auth before browser or device-code\nCLI login begins.\n- Remove superseded-token detection and revocation from the shared token\npersistence path; successful login now only saves the new credentials.\n- Read the raw configured auth store during CLI cleanup so\nenvironment-provided auth cannot mask the stored refresh token.\n- Preserve `auto` storage fallback semantics when keyring deletion fails\nby clearing the fallback auth file.\n- Add a process-level CLI regression test that requires the revoke\nrequest to precede every device-login request and occur exactly once.\n\nIf replacement login is canceled or fails, the previous local\ncredentials have already been cleared. Remote revocation remains best\neffort, matching explicit logout behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n### Process-level before/after reproduction\n\nI compiled the real `codex` CLI from the pre-fix parent (`14df0e8833`)\nand from the PR implementation (`25c002f23b`; the login behavior is\nunchanged at the current head), then ran the same device-code flow\nagainst a local HTTP mock OAuth authority.\n\nEach run:\n\n1. Used a fresh temporary `CODEX_HOME` configured with\n`cli_auth_credentials_store = \"file\"`.\n2. Seeded that temporary home with managed ChatGPT auth containing\n`old-access` and `old-refresh` tokens.\n3. Pointed `CODEX_REVOKE_TOKEN_URL_OVERRIDE` at the mock `/oauth/revoke`\nendpoint.\n4. Ran the compiled CLI as:\n\n   ```shell\n   CODEX_HOME=<temporary-home> \\\n     CODEX_REVOKE_TOKEN_URL_OVERRIDE=<mock-issuer>/oauth/revoke \\\n<compiled-codex> login --device-auth --experimental_issuer <mock-issuer>\n   ```\n\n5. Recorded every request received by the mock authority. The mock\nmarked `new-access` valid when `/oauth/token` issued it and invalidated\nit if `/oauth/revoke` arrived afterward, reproducing the observed\nsession-invalidating failure mode. After login exited, the harness also\nverified the persisted refresh token and probed a protected endpoint\nwith `new-access`.\n\n| Build | Observed request order | CLI/persistence result | `new-access`\nprobe |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Pre-fix | `usercode → device token → OAuth token →\nrevoke(old-refresh)` | Exit `0`; `new-refresh` persisted | `401` |\n| PR | `revoke(old-refresh) → usercode → device token → OAuth token` |\nExit `0`; `new-refresh` persisted | `200` |\n\nThe PR run therefore issued exactly one revocation request, before any\nrequest that initiated the replacement login, and issued no revocation\nafter token exchange.\n\n### Regression coverage\n\n\n`codex-rs/cli/tests/login.rs::device_login_revokes_existing_auth_before_requesting_new_tokens`\nruns the real first-party `codex` binary against a `wiremock` OAuth\nserver with an isolated temporary `CODEX_HOME`. It asserts:\n\n- the exact request sequence is `/oauth/revoke`,\n`/api/accounts/deviceauth/usercode`, `/api/accounts/deviceauth/token`,\nthen `/oauth/token`;\n- there is exactly one revoke request and its body contains\n`old-refresh` with the `refresh_token` hint;\n- the completed login persists `new-refresh`.\n\nLocal validation:\n\n- `just test -p codex-login` — 130 passed\n- `just test -p codex-cli` — 280 passed, including the new process-level\nregression test\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","tree":{"sha":"3884da9c1645380eb51310a6cd6ebd4d75a2a0b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3884da9c1645380eb51310a6cd6ebd4d75a2a0b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d1aaf789ade6b0f20d746e7fa7ac8a7520798456","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLGA2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn9oQACb5ZNP1c9fgPnH2ywqfWwDg\nZ+SbcELUTe2crQqnU9heVUDHaWYpPIJVIForKAOSze8TYpj5zYDywwROsa4i24UZ\nfYhwV+Fp03+PFcOGEgu4Kyg/emEuQKff4Z3/iW3JyWQ90l6rvjjC+/UagMe/FBNW\n/oVGM2rYH9OY5RmC8RhL9EkG6nfPh8ZMEJXDfC4Plmrx18Cyf1FHRuiCYw/hkyG+\ni3gGFYbkNruFIfBYWaQb1usoFFdzi60HHqskc0g2rziQ6zLVOfWE9DULDP1tdH4d\nmirERJydACJd6VzOTPQf3ytE0S0Y0utBEzEuSdJsYvz0yQ8du7RURDQHXc9knz5O\ncs/DX9w9Z7kcwP5IL9ArAesOqQsWUgfwR6PttPLvo2dH0jpnuwlA1nCO69aFiKXC\nfB1sXBgLVJczLiPbej7v1YNPMync0QW1d1zKiUcrHEsNQbcHGsE94LKR4v+U/t47\nxS0gsupLFxTlvscKqtijmP705OPKN0KcptYlcrwL8eCiAvIHbXb0HgGI3g1iK+ll\njGfuYojd9FvE4sq+tM/l6xFgc9BxatL7rTljjVwSNzI4rb1Ejs6hmnU18g3QRffz\nkmORbQfTUETxagoml4Li3U1g7i0fOQwKhHdTgwCtmfVeQZMi3P5NdgYnK+1BRMOV\neoBMKBoId7oOgIDp46Oj\n=94kX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3884da9c1645380eb51310a6cd6ebd4d75a2a0b1\nparent b724f5966ee020b2d6675975bc96cfaf5ee243cb\nauthor cooper-oai <cooper@openai.com> 1781293110 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781293110 -0700\n\n[login] revoke existing auth before starting login (#27674)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex login` previously persisted newly issued OAuth credentials and\nonly then attempted to revoke the superseded refresh token. The old\ncredential must be revoked before a replacement browser or device-code\nflow starts, and successful login must not perform any post-login\nrevocation attempt.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Revoke and clear existing stored auth before browser or device-code\nCLI login begins.\n- Remove superseded-token detection and revocation from the shared token\npersistence path; successful login now only saves the new credentials.\n- Read the raw configured auth store during CLI cleanup so\nenvironment-provided auth cannot mask the stored refresh token.\n- Preserve `auto` storage fallback semantics when keyring deletion fails\nby clearing the fallback auth file.\n- Add a process-level CLI regression test that requires the revoke\nrequest to precede every device-login request and occur exactly once.\n\nIf replacement login is canceled or fails, the previous local\ncredentials have already been cleared. Remote revocation remains best\neffort, matching explicit logout behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n### Process-level before/after reproduction\n\nI compiled the real `codex` CLI from the pre-fix parent (`14df0e8833`)\nand from the PR implementation (`25c002f23b`; the login behavior is\nunchanged at the current head), then ran the same device-code flow\nagainst a local HTTP mock OAuth authority.\n\nEach run:\n\n1. Used a fresh temporary `CODEX_HOME` configured with\n`cli_auth_credentials_store = \"file\"`.\n2. Seeded that temporary home with managed ChatGPT auth containing\n`old-access` and `old-refresh` tokens.\n3. Pointed `CODEX_REVOKE_TOKEN_URL_OVERRIDE` at the mock `/oauth/revoke`\nendpoint.\n4. Ran the compiled CLI as:\n\n   ```shell\n   CODEX_HOME=<temporary-home> \\\n     CODEX_REVOKE_TOKEN_URL_OVERRIDE=<mock-issuer>/oauth/revoke \\\n<compiled-codex> login --device-auth --experimental_issuer <mock-issuer>\n   ```\n\n5. Recorded every request received by the mock authority. The mock\nmarked `new-access` valid when `/oauth/token` issued it and invalidated\nit if `/oauth/revoke` arrived afterward, reproducing the observed\nsession-invalidating failure mode. After login exited, the harness also\nverified the persisted refresh token and probed a protected endpoint\nwith `new-access`.\n\n| Build | Observed request order | CLI/persistence result | `new-access`\nprobe |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Pre-fix | `usercode → device token → OAuth token →\nrevoke(old-refresh)` | Exit `0`; `new-refresh` persisted | `401` |\n| PR | `revoke(old-refresh) → usercode → device token → OAuth token` |\nExit `0`; `new-refresh` persisted | `200` |\n\nThe PR run therefore issued exactly one revocation request, before any\nrequest that initiated the replacement login, and issued no revocation\nafter token exchange.\n\n### Regression coverage\n\n\n`codex-rs/cli/tests/login.rs::device_login_revokes_existing_auth_before_requesting_new_tokens`\nruns the real first-party `codex` binary against a `wiremock` OAuth\nserver with an isolated temporary `CODEX_HOME`. It asserts:\n\n- the exact request sequence is `/oauth/revoke`,\n`/api/accounts/deviceauth/usercode`, `/api/accounts/deviceauth/token`,\nthen `/oauth/token`;\n- there is exactly one revoke request and its body contains\n`old-refresh` with the `refresh_token` hint;\n- the completed login persists `new-refresh`.\n\nLocal validation:\n\n- `just test -p codex-login` — 130 passed\n- `just test -p codex-cli` — 280 passed, including the new process-level\nregression test\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","verified_at":"2026-06-12T19:38:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d1aaf789ade6b0f20d746e7fa7ac8a7520798456","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d1aaf789ade6b0f20d746e7fa7ac8a7520798456","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d1aaf789ade6b0f20d746e7fa7ac8a7520798456/comments","author":{"login":"cooper-oai","id":242064477,"node_id":"U_kgDODm2cXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/242064477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/cooper-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b724f5966ee020b2d6675975bc96cfaf5ee243cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b724f5966ee020b2d6675975bc96cfaf5ee243cb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b724f5966ee020b2d6675975bc96cfaf5ee243cb"}]},{"sha":"b724f5966ee020b2d6675975bc96cfaf5ee243cb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI3MjRmNTk2NmVlMDIwYjJkNjY3NTk3NWJjOTZjZmFmNWVlMjQzY2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T19:15:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T19:15:21Z"},"message":"feat: add secret auth storage configuration (#27504)\n\n## Why\n\nWindows Credential Manager limits generic credential blobs to 2,560\nbytes. The encrypted local secrets backend avoids storing large\nserialized auth payloads directly in the OS keyring, but selecting that\nbackend needs an independently reviewable feature/config layer before\nthe auth and secrets implementation is wired in.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added the stable `secret_auth_storage` feature, enabled by default on\nWindows and disabled by default elsewhere.\n- Added `AuthKeyringBackendKind` and config resolution for full and\nbootstrap config loading.\n- Applied managed feature requirements when resolving the bootstrap auth\nbackend.\n- Updated the generated config schema and added focused tests.\n\nThis is the base PR for #17931. The auth, secrets, MCP, CLI, TUI, and\napp-server implementation remains in that follow-up PR.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresolve_bootstrap_auth_keyring_backend_kind_uses_secret_auth_storage_feature`\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n\nThe full `just test -p codex-core` run compiled successfully and ran\n2,690 tests; 2,589 passed, one was flaky, and 101 environment-sensitive\ntests failed because this shell injects a `pyenv` rehash warning into\ncommand output or because sandboxed subprocesses timed out.","tree":{"sha":"695c6540b01c5f3d33d78c67992feebeeb904a37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/695c6540b01c5f3d33d78c67992feebeeb904a37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b724f5966ee020b2d6675975bc96cfaf5ee243cb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLFrJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJjYQAAhlzg4MmwkdMll785K2xrJA\nhykvWJdWjTqK6mPi4HbOAkpEnUB5CcvgEGj6hWFQGYf2yHZmCG0zWPClymOGSkAL\nt9Y2rNm6JA+YLQ8jawuKEbTF/wleBUfq6Cm1nMYlPyHuCYtOO5QQd0ZwPQ4g/0Tc\nj399eci7Qh19a9xaJFYDXuB/kXjEtmuKTRZ6SfSE3Tudj5Tbt/0Bwek2v83sFUgR\nHuGF+HDGNmGESuh0hqG/RUPgPj4OeK7z4kBgwfH47k05vnqDHeU4odtBoAqA5cUY\ng549AFr8mx4NUX+NL8RtrIIfjkhdYIuEwJ4FunwiatKsDoDiTrnw2iP1qZhhVLPI\nmDPQJN3uEpAYhnLWkcieA/6Gwso7t0e48cNkN09JXymIp+dEZGT5uNM/WK0kC4BC\navjevvQKE6v4G0sAHJ2GIDGR8/QI3ainK/qEzZidNMfENvaMVd32VR+NXsF0+5BZ\n6Jdq9hDLKElbaFuO9NbtXQ79sgxJ2hyzYtcMaAov1TcjPmYwk3GYvOUdqeFDz+RK\n0rqMSCcIcHF9gyotJLDkdX97ULiSks0fSjuV4hmoxHuMaEq7jHQSibvUWk7vRVKg\n5Q7uRN5znJQvYDtTY1HHQeXwfK3FkvR8RG+c1K9lh9woYZtIh25LurjR6OQFuKE6\n2LZa6HJ7pYfD5KK+ud1H\n=6SWM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 695c6540b01c5f3d33d78c67992feebeeb904a37\nparent 76d8f20241ad83137785cea0e29674f45472e4dd\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1781291721 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781291721 +0000\n\nfeat: add secret auth storage configuration (#27504)\n\n## Why\n\nWindows Credential Manager limits generic credential blobs to 2,560\nbytes. The encrypted local secrets backend avoids storing large\nserialized auth payloads directly in the OS keyring, but selecting that\nbackend needs an independently reviewable feature/config layer before\nthe auth and secrets implementation is wired in.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added the stable `secret_auth_storage` feature, enabled by default on\nWindows and disabled by default elsewhere.\n- Added `AuthKeyringBackendKind` and config resolution for full and\nbootstrap config loading.\n- Applied managed feature requirements when resolving the bootstrap auth\nbackend.\n- Updated the generated config schema and added focused tests.\n\nThis is the base PR for #17931. The auth, secrets, MCP, CLI, TUI, and\napp-server implementation remains in that follow-up PR.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresolve_bootstrap_auth_keyring_backend_kind_uses_secret_auth_storage_feature`\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n\nThe full `just test -p codex-core` run compiled successfully and ran\n2,690 tests; 2,589 passed, one was flaky, and 101 environment-sensitive\ntests failed because this shell injects a `pyenv` rehash warning into\ncommand output or because sandboxed subprocesses timed out.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T19:15:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b724f5966ee020b2d6675975bc96cfaf5ee243cb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b724f5966ee020b2d6675975bc96cfaf5ee243cb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b724f5966ee020b2d6675975bc96cfaf5ee243cb/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"76d8f20241ad83137785cea0e29674f45472e4dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/76d8f20241ad83137785cea0e29674f45472e4dd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/76d8f20241ad83137785cea0e29674f45472e4dd"}]},{"sha":"76d8f20241ad83137785cea0e29674f45472e4dd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc2ZDhmMjAyNDFhZDgzMTM3Nzg1Y2VhMGUyOTY3NGY0NTQ3MmU0ZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T19:12:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T19:12:08Z"},"message":"[codex] Add size to internal filesystem metadata (#27927)\n\n## Why\n\n`ExecutorFileSystem::get_metadata` reports file kind and timestamps but\nnot size. Internal callers that need to enforce a size limit therefore\nhave to read the complete file first, which is especially wasteful for\nremote filesystems.\n\nThis adds the missing internal metadata so consumers can reject\noversized files before transferring or buffering them. The field is\nnamed `size`, matching VS Code's `FileStat.size` filesystem convention.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add `size: u64` to internal `FileMetadata`\n- populate it from the underlying filesystem metadata\n- carry it through sandbox-helper and remote exec-server responses\n- cover files, directories, symlink targets, and sandboxed reads across\nlocal and remote filesystem implementations\n\nThe new field is intentionally not exposed through the app-server API.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server get_metadata`\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server\nfile_system_sandboxed_metadata_and_read_allow_readable_root`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-skills-extension`","tree":{"sha":"4976d007299a37c461793270213425a14c44675b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4976d007299a37c461793270213425a14c44675b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/76d8f20241ad83137785cea0e29674f45472e4dd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLFoICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARNcQAByy/I0B4zJxDM/1JSU1KP2o\n09cvGXduEhMwCrcWt9sjaIinhYUTySh9Cgew6godxOrKC/wF6qv8J2MxsYagsbDZ\nDZ99e58FjGbjkwVvkdDGPbLSM/ARmRvL9gOVpmwUEyy6WSh8Mrnhdfj4v1i9Og7Y\nPobuCsbHFPgEEd5Do6mUy1CgpVIBgeP/kP+2tMesh659v0NtWh5JnmaajjL5bRjx\nFLwrwJfVmukfUJiKEiYRnpvqtB3LaJOAqhKr7TaXBj/mBbEdVZzjdm6K7nyOSAyG\nxgo2rkxHRxqdhEPHX9VFT8D6WifuA8BrSM4jM2sCfBJ1qTc5mrCfmwdX7yEKzDVD\nQKRDXB6kZoZ29UFsw7kvgm0qcp9EftLmgTxOzZ5Y5t9JIvSDttkkn+JFJHmCzMhU\nkCITQNajjITPlaLyWO/4HSFn+JbKTMORLIZCLPdAYtyNSDcGjWLVpwZ56Skx6b5z\nA71MvQ/U6a1HXxjr2AxFLOOgRS67J9O6awVjczPCQzgDG9LMcODQo++7SZLeagLW\nskN9oXJHRpfSkq5hxmwEeB10pVPfmw7O9smmzaM9uxSgURFT7LsEEbn8frrdcIbI\n1gqLDJgmWhPDI3pVMiLXo2zWD7ehW8TDJqHs0ibwlLs6prfTmLyT+sKe31ED8VdR\n2k443J9LDw5b06s+bgUy\n=IONm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4976d007299a37c461793270213425a14c44675b\nparent b6baa77eec6838a5a4af0ae16d03f13cd6315d1e\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781291528 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781291528 -0700\n\n[codex] Add size to internal filesystem metadata (#27927)\n\n## Why\n\n`ExecutorFileSystem::get_metadata` reports file kind and timestamps but\nnot size. Internal callers that need to enforce a size limit therefore\nhave to read the complete file first, which is especially wasteful for\nremote filesystems.\n\nThis adds the missing internal metadata so consumers can reject\noversized files before transferring or buffering them. The field is\nnamed `size`, matching VS Code's `FileStat.size` filesystem convention.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add `size: u64` to internal `FileMetadata`\n- populate it from the underlying filesystem metadata\n- carry it through sandbox-helper and remote exec-server responses\n- cover files, directories, symlink targets, and sandboxed reads across\nlocal and remote filesystem implementations\n\nThe new field is intentionally not exposed through the app-server API.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server get_metadata`\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server\nfile_system_sandboxed_metadata_and_read_allow_readable_root`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-skills-extension`","verified_at":"2026-06-12T19:12:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/76d8f20241ad83137785cea0e29674f45472e4dd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/76d8f20241ad83137785cea0e29674f45472e4dd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/76d8f20241ad83137785cea0e29674f45472e4dd/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b6baa77eec6838a5a4af0ae16d03f13cd6315d1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b6baa77eec6838a5a4af0ae16d03f13cd6315d1e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b6baa77eec6838a5a4af0ae16d03f13cd6315d1e"}]},{"sha":"b6baa77eec6838a5a4af0ae16d03f13cd6315d1e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI2YmFhNzdlZWM2ODM4YTVhNGFmMGFlMTZkMDNmMTNjZDYzMTVkMWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:57:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:57:22Z"},"message":"Handle standalone image generation failures as terminal items (#27920)\n\n## Why\n\nStandalone image generation emitted a started item but no terminal item\nwhen the backend failed. Clients could leave the operation unresolved or\nrender it as successful.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Emit a terminal image-generation item with `status: \"failed\"` when\ngeneration or editing fails.\n- Skip image persistence for failed terminal items.\n- Render failed image generation distinctly in TUI history.\n- Preserve the status when handling live and replayed terminal items.\n\n## Looks for TUI, App-Side change needed \n\n<img width=\"867\" height=\"89\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9e32342f-a982-411e-8498-456639fc468a\"\n/>\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- App-server image-generation tests\n- Core stream-event tests\n- TUI image-generation lifecycle and snapshot tests\n- Scoped Clippy and formatting","tree":{"sha":"6594bd92d27c211a6021b0bbb7b5ca322baa80a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6594bd92d27c211a6021b0bbb7b5ca322baa80a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b6baa77eec6838a5a4af0ae16d03f13cd6315d1e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLFaSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMLMQAIfdHAJIE/fYEKlJS+59YGDY\njDIeRGkpXeoYFmca/VEZxrXgI5MRdnF3rQ05UIEt/TklDrRXFboCaUuQ5aGU3Ap4\n/wgHTlizkA7e6+2Dq6aXSZvPmh6Q9vVnwjxui0+737YL1XKrc+iHSY+v6CUmFMO5\nUIoEO84dFMRo182bIkXl9jkpAzCfpZIqktEGBHymjgJv8Tf4pPRIGUdWXBuuAdIp\ngVSMxHQLN/VZhQMbTl7rfXQVX144UateqVHOk0iAnk25UIak53XFOEvuu97/mNbX\ne0VUwb+IfWpEx0V1JBkCrvrmq7+uZjDqwdcW9K6YPzHv/yqdbpnhTFh1HaNU15v4\njW55++cdb4PSlJADIQyR9HaBWD6ecgtNsNul+IcRD80bfcqxiENFOycNaWEAB8s0\nMZWiHjlDDztUog6J5yEiswiYjgtq19cFe4Ku0sg0cNeMTJFkAcyUSD09TXLiwdj7\nXpQ3HuwsLJnQ577/gJoWtCxbk1ZMCoqyqoaAozfu4ESdQG43zoJkTffH+XMdpcRM\nh1N/D7jUR72Fde2210KxNZjDMx1OEVsTb4yuJq2vlMTFrUKdzZ2qYl/cTBvYpVdq\nFYD3ySy2dvNC6A0khoHQd7hmG/LOyPgc78W5+cHpDPV7DZFzcYxA1Ux8QbhtMI97\nNYf09FEixOJvTCGzFRs0\n=rb6H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6594bd92d27c211a6021b0bbb7b5ca322baa80a3\nparent e26f734f919819bdd802b1b67ad653863c7a90e5\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1781290642 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781290642 -0700\n\nHandle standalone image generation failures as terminal items (#27920)\n\n## Why\n\nStandalone image generation emitted a started item but no terminal item\nwhen the backend failed. Clients could leave the operation unresolved or\nrender it as successful.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Emit a terminal image-generation item with `status: \"failed\"` when\ngeneration or editing fails.\n- Skip image persistence for failed terminal items.\n- Render failed image generation distinctly in TUI history.\n- Preserve the status when handling live and replayed terminal items.\n\n## Looks for TUI, App-Side change needed \n\n<img width=\"867\" height=\"89\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9e32342f-a982-411e-8498-456639fc468a\"\n/>\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- App-server image-generation tests\n- Core stream-event tests\n- TUI image-generation lifecycle and snapshot tests\n- Scoped Clippy and formatting","verified_at":"2026-06-12T18:57:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b6baa77eec6838a5a4af0ae16d03f13cd6315d1e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b6baa77eec6838a5a4af0ae16d03f13cd6315d1e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b6baa77eec6838a5a4af0ae16d03f13cd6315d1e/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e26f734f919819bdd802b1b67ad653863c7a90e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e26f734f919819bdd802b1b67ad653863c7a90e5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e26f734f919819bdd802b1b67ad653863c7a90e5"}]},{"sha":"e26f734f919819bdd802b1b67ad653863c7a90e5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUyNmY3MzRmOTE5ODE5YmRkODAyYjFiNjdhZDY1Mzg2M2M3YTkwZTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:54:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:54:28Z"},"message":"[codex] unify apply patch parsing (#27913)\n\n## Why\n\n`apply_patch` maintained separate batch and streaming parsers for the\nsame patch grammar. That duplicated the parsing rules and allowed final\nexecution to disagree with the live streamed preview.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Make `StreamingPatchParser` the single owner of hunk and environment\nID parsing.\n- Keep heredoc and outer patch-boundary normalization in the existing\n`parse_patch` wrapper, preserving its public API.\n- Reject non-whitespace content after `*** End Patch` and preserve\nseparator handling after `*** End of File`.\n- Reject duplicate environment ID preambles explicitly.\n- Remove the duplicate batch hunk parser and its implementation-specific\ntests.\n\nThe change removes 201 net lines while retaining focused coverage for\nthe unified parser's boundary behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-apply-patch`\n- Compared a 24-hour corpus of 2,788,059 observed `apply_patch` payloads\nagainst the previous batch parser. All 2,779,502 accepted payloads\nproduced identical hunks, canonical patch text, and environment IDs; the\nremaining 8,557 payloads were rejected by both parsers, with zero\nacceptance or payload mismatches.","tree":{"sha":"32da079b085e770850627fc119132f192da204a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/32da079b085e770850627fc119132f192da204a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e26f734f919819bdd802b1b67ad653863c7a90e5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLFXkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADD0QAA8g4av3SBH3WrkMwuX1gmQd\nz2I04sR1oHW/V30T6WA3ZKjBU3f8itwM/KSwYV96a+Erg640AbvikNvfrv+CFlnr\n7xq6Z8JlvF3tu/Z0fa8nT1TM1kVHw+zrE6litiZ4+j/VYucIsyPo3MB+f+CoVPwj\n2fHut8HS6LwsMA6HdentFw/hcPOGHY1/N06m6Yt25hMjkyfPCyln3fMPtOfG1Z8S\nXJiUXBDDNGBqXzD+/GAbHepLXMo9MXxpbLgt9pHqtB5r6ClZfqY/bjyn26yGXBWK\nyXfQmhfrI3WgW9DeVsrN3x2ZF2+YmHp0hT3gujzZa23+FyxmQ1yzR8guVzXmFPlK\na30E7NzMayZMQp58ffqX1q5eJIDQ3gR+RZkY7Wt+5tatOo2clXBic5M8bKcggCXM\nR3yyFZ5xbZrOtFLDWAKF3SzFIUuQgapwVElTTTThYOBTkPY7lTPMb+Xf6Jg7TWZq\nmxe+UC46Gl837C2S8iFK30c1bHQ3Yz8pzvfp2H579yd28rLpAXMQJu+8OkrMinrX\nsBhq6pMoHIqyLG/5fj5t7VmekFq/4lLQ4/OlmQn756829rGRW1VrHpYy+UPdGEAh\nfxvkZz3kLyI9b70d3gc6sXs5ETTCbeCMWGQzrVtevhErUzPbI1UfG7756JruRXte\nSR8ZgGR0S/sVoX+hjuVI\n=fjoF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 32da079b085e770850627fc119132f192da204a2\nparent 9600afb1a1196df66667f42fa26df4fac71ee22c\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781290468 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781290468 -0700\n\n[codex] unify apply patch parsing (#27913)\n\n## Why\n\n`apply_patch` maintained separate batch and streaming parsers for the\nsame patch grammar. That duplicated the parsing rules and allowed final\nexecution to disagree with the live streamed preview.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Make `StreamingPatchParser` the single owner of hunk and environment\nID parsing.\n- Keep heredoc and outer patch-boundary normalization in the existing\n`parse_patch` wrapper, preserving its public API.\n- Reject non-whitespace content after `*** End Patch` and preserve\nseparator handling after `*** End of File`.\n- Reject duplicate environment ID preambles explicitly.\n- Remove the duplicate batch hunk parser and its implementation-specific\ntests.\n\nThe change removes 201 net lines while retaining focused coverage for\nthe unified parser's boundary behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-apply-patch`\n- Compared a 24-hour corpus of 2,788,059 observed `apply_patch` payloads\nagainst the previous batch parser. All 2,779,502 accepted payloads\nproduced identical hunks, canonical patch text, and environment IDs; the\nremaining 8,557 payloads were rejected by both parsers, with zero\nacceptance or payload mismatches.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T18:54:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e26f734f919819bdd802b1b67ad653863c7a90e5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e26f734f919819bdd802b1b67ad653863c7a90e5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e26f734f919819bdd802b1b67ad653863c7a90e5/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9600afb1a1196df66667f42fa26df4fac71ee22c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9600afb1a1196df66667f42fa26df4fac71ee22c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9600afb1a1196df66667f42fa26df4fac71ee22c"}]},{"sha":"9600afb1a1196df66667f42fa26df4fac71ee22c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk2MDBhZmIxYTExOTZkZjY2NjY3ZjQyZmEyNmRmNGZhYzcxZWUyMmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Ning","email":"ericning@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:53:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:53:55Z"},"message":"[codex] expose remote plugin share URL (#27890)\n\n## Summary\n\n- expose the remote plugin detail endpoint's `share_url` as nullable\n`PluginDetail.shareUrl`\n- preserve existing `PluginSummary.shareContext` behavior for local and\nworkspace sharing flows\n- regenerate the app-server TypeScript and JSON schema fixtures\n\n## Why\n\nThe remote plugin detail response already includes a canonical\n`share_url`, but that value was not surfaced by `plugin/read` for global\nplugins. Global plugins intentionally have no `shareContext`, so using\nthat model for the URL would change the semantics consumed by the\nexisting share modal.\n\n## User impact\n\nCodex clients can use `PluginDetail.shareUrl` for a remote plugin's\ncopy-link action, including when the plugin is disabled by an\nadministrator, without changing existing share-modal or ownership\nbehavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_read_includes_share_url_for_admin_disabled_remote_plugin`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol\ntypescript_schema_fixtures_match_generated`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol\njson_schema_fixtures_match_generated`\n- `cargo fmt --all`","tree":{"sha":"239e4dd58cd86c145d3ff78705d811ba7c7fed5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/239e4dd58cd86c145d3ff78705d811ba7c7fed5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9600afb1a1196df66667f42fa26df4fac71ee22c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLFXDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjNIQAF0AKYgDU3KWG86VtXMhJTn4\nJuuUPrZzx5IcJ5NO8R18RMloWujY3UL5eQOuTMzni6E/cSe5tnoF2TAJV/odoX9q\nS2rDjLF/XQlpyaibLZBmfBcy9IgK8HWurqYb59a3z718aU+y0yZBlptF0QphON32\nZg4ycCDOLLNQkikcK717Mn6ytlFsvq37Zbp+sj3/gUPLkgX5MzrlsC9oidgBMEDl\neKdULH4tW+x7B4rzMkjiP0BfcX6XvbMr5nnssNpaBz+gRS/Uc8w6WE7SnBXx2DHW\nrliUMgBwApN5MqN4Rk9hZDThLO9aYueOXxsMcRWK98ivb/g7KQaTpYbyjBO4Crdm\nZfTkRueZoc9C6VMIaLuVyqkygsLnM+r0YKHMOYGbI67FPz5ABALo0BKRx0qxgG8r\nTnj+Xiy0YHyJ0ing3DTF7LxN5iVCNT1EHkLBauAaOt2J98ZY0PDnoBr9IS+wTgZY\n2JFjiEOwf+6+KPy616i98obWOYdtGfEpQpVV7RThVa3Tr/VqhmED1Od5Yvv9tT58\nc5YDMIlN1Z6Kbsh/a7+Uv5TgYJA1HSM7bYeZKK44qK0gCNPOUHnlyBtWAcxttcz3\neW5uYzqvFm80e1k9zPu/f9MjWok2eNYRG4pkhmlJgd+88l0GFhecHPRpT3DHy/h3\nNeqo1aKUneoUSaQDoSYY\n=jlAD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 239e4dd58cd86c145d3ff78705d811ba7c7fed5f\nparent 52a50aec709d1934522d7ebdd9ceb4dc75c198f9\nauthor Eric Ning <ericning@openai.com> 1781290435 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781290435 -0700\n\n[codex] expose remote plugin share URL (#27890)\n\n## Summary\n\n- expose the remote plugin detail endpoint's `share_url` as nullable\n`PluginDetail.shareUrl`\n- preserve existing `PluginSummary.shareContext` behavior for local and\nworkspace sharing flows\n- regenerate the app-server TypeScript and JSON schema fixtures\n\n## Why\n\nThe remote plugin detail response already includes a canonical\n`share_url`, but that value was not surfaced by `plugin/read` for global\nplugins. Global plugins intentionally have no `shareContext`, so using\nthat model for the URL would change the semantics consumed by the\nexisting share modal.\n\n## User impact\n\nCodex clients can use `PluginDetail.shareUrl` for a remote plugin's\ncopy-link action, including when the plugin is disabled by an\nadministrator, without changing existing share-modal or ownership\nbehavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_read_includes_share_url_for_admin_disabled_remote_plugin`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol\ntypescript_schema_fixtures_match_generated`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol\njson_schema_fixtures_match_generated`\n- `cargo fmt --all`","verified_at":"2026-06-12T18:53:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9600afb1a1196df66667f42fa26df4fac71ee22c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9600afb1a1196df66667f42fa26df4fac71ee22c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9600afb1a1196df66667f42fa26df4fac71ee22c/comments","author":{"login":"ericning-o","id":182030612,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtmRFA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182030612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o","html_url":"https://github.com/ericning-o","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"52a50aec709d1934522d7ebdd9ceb4dc75c198f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52a50aec709d1934522d7ebdd9ceb4dc75c198f9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/52a50aec709d1934522d7ebdd9ceb4dc75c198f9"}]},{"sha":"52a50aec709d1934522d7ebdd9ceb4dc75c198f9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUyYTUwYWVjNzA5ZDE5MzQ1MjJkN2ViZGQ5Y2ViNGRjNzVjMTk4Zjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:38:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:38:01Z"},"message":"sandboxing: migrate cwd inputs to PathUri (#27816)\n\n## Why\n\nSandbox cwd values can cross app-server and exec-server host boundaries.\nThey should retain URI semantics until the receiving host validates them\ninstead of being interpreted early as native paths.\n\n## What\n\n- Carry `PathUri` through filesystem sandbox contexts, sandbox commands,\nand transform inputs.\n- Convert command and policy cwd once in `SandboxManager::transform`,\nthen keep launch requests native.\n- Preserve sandbox cwd over remote filesystem transport and reject\nnon-native URIs without fallback.\n- Cache paired native/URI turn-environment cwd values during migration,\nwith immutable access to keep them synchronized.\n- Extend existing protocol, forwarding, transform, and core runtime\ntests.","tree":{"sha":"fb90b54dd4817c21818fb281a3a83952e37d01ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/fb90b54dd4817c21818fb281a3a83952e37d01ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/52a50aec709d1934522d7ebdd9ceb4dc75c198f9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLFIJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJdoQAFetHTfh+SaFRZOJ97Y5H52Z\noSkjcrzau30WhLHmsqdu1EErNAch7pTDamIA3JRbDBK/VyLPgNABX3tvepaSSaFW\nQsn5P87iaL2Bn4WOV7fOEtoBk5YfwWJ4w+w7+eq77g12JHjUuMwC16cJq9qLeHXN\ndbs6Jcrkqcp6gxa7XzZqatvcJBdSFkGZCK2UqD2J2klnZ0o/TG5j7hGvaXH31zeh\nEaQdf7g5Q/+PwMayOf8NmKQvQhdfWRapJN71slygktBxEUkHEhV1t5x30+PiXqO9\ni0qKnaL0YH5c+fkpbEQk5gmD3mHA0pnoJjX2Pu1RLpuCybdGuRUb37HADlaGIxfE\nYbh3/GfTveXgoAohmpQxgF5wY6Mnrc0aNFbhcnRQv2TekHa/hi+/qgK85L4CsTFS\nymv7M7/SDUiAKeRfCu44dXpF1hDxzFl45bSE9EMGp3J3v20qcTd09aak3VjFliY9\nw5VMZsS6orrMfHeX7bZU1plvyieVXC9baCXjYExnhI00hVSwlPdbAeHB2UMxMyNj\nCxc05+7hFnGy/BtX+bYi2mPo5qLWkAl/Qyl1eKSu8nn0eaJtL7mzeEsfavGW4oaa\nQVl6BDEIoxYWyS50NQ80arHYyXBx0wlLvqNoSqZis0epzV2HUboU+06W72+JXiM+\nNUNooJp4zUtd0LWMC5Dj\n=OzLX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fb90b54dd4817c21818fb281a3a83952e37d01ea\nparent 84520225b9928a9eee3ed2c9072fb5d26d6fc6e6\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781289481 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781289481 -0700\n\nsandboxing: migrate cwd inputs to PathUri (#27816)\n\n## Why\n\nSandbox cwd values can cross app-server and exec-server host boundaries.\nThey should retain URI semantics until the receiving host validates them\ninstead of being interpreted early as native paths.\n\n## What\n\n- Carry `PathUri` through filesystem sandbox contexts, sandbox commands,\nand transform inputs.\n- Convert command and policy cwd once in `SandboxManager::transform`,\nthen keep launch requests native.\n- Preserve sandbox cwd over remote filesystem transport and reject\nnon-native URIs without fallback.\n- Cache paired native/URI turn-environment cwd values during migration,\nwith immutable access to keep them synchronized.\n- Extend existing protocol, forwarding, transform, and core runtime\ntests.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T18:38:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52a50aec709d1934522d7ebdd9ceb4dc75c198f9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/52a50aec709d1934522d7ebdd9ceb4dc75c198f9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52a50aec709d1934522d7ebdd9ceb4dc75c198f9/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}"